{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c46f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":146,"recorded_at":1780531400000287,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c45b-2ac5-7ab1-ba69-88ee1187dbcb"},"task_id":"01a0c45b-2ac5-7ab1-ba69-88ee1187dbcb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c45b-2ac5-7ab1-ba69-88ee1187dbcb","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev3.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev2.md and TASK-260830-35urbp_producer.md. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-35urbp, the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i. Revision 2 was reviewed by RUN-260921-5a9d4b (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED with **no P1**: one P2 class and five P3. Read TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev2.md first. The reviewer states that **every rev1 P1/P2/P3 finding is closed with driven evidence** — the Windows vet compile, the forked attestation model (you now consume the landed admission), the nine surviving mutants, the Windows tmux claim, the decision-core bound, the dead inputs. Keep all of it and change nothing that the verdict grades closed. Production is correct on this tree at every point below; this rework is tests, one small gate decision, and honest prose.\n3|Trunk has NOT moved (base is still 799c338). Your working tree is the rev2 candidate; build revision 3 on it. Do not refresh, do not rebase.\n4|\n5|1. **P2-A, the only P2 — the verify-side \"non-directory leaf\" refusal is unpinned, and it is the entry the background path uses.** Row 5 names `EnsureRuntimeDir` only. The verify side implements the same refusal through `O_DIRECTORY` on `verifyRuntimeDir`'s `Openat` (runtime_unix.go:105-106), and `Acquire` uses that side on the background path (acquire.go:168). The reviewer dropped `O_DIRECTORY` from the verify `Openat` alone (`R01-verify-odirectory`, keeping `O_NOFOLLOW`) and it SURVIVED the committed suite in both passes: a regular 0700 file at `root/ax-tmux` makes `VerifyRuntimeDir` return nil, and a FIFO at the leaf makes it **block for the full 5s deadline**, because the verify `Openat` carries no `O_NONBLOCK` — the exact hang class the landed `secprim.openNoFollow` comment documents. This is the rev1 finding \"the verify side follows a symlink leaf\" recurring one member over: the symlink member got its verify-side test and its harness row, the non-directory member did not. Ship: a committed `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` covering a regular file AND a FIFO under a deadline so the no-hang property is pinned too, the same shape driven through the background `Acquire`, and a harness row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` that drops the flag on the verify `Openat` only. Update row 5 to name both entries. While you are there, decide deliberately whether the verify `Openat` should carry `O_NONBLOCK` like the landed helper does — if you leave it off, the FIFO deadline test must pin the current behaviour and TRACEABILITY must say which.\n6|2. **P3-A — both-empty generation arms are unmeasured on two exported entries.** `CheckServerAttested`'s `wantGeneration == \"\"` disjunct (readiness.go:43) and `CheckBrokerContact`'s `report.Principal.Generation == \"\"` disjunct (readiness.go:83) both survive deletion: every committed row keeps one side non-empty, so `\"\" != \"generation-7\"` refuses with or without the arm. Through `Acquire` the both-empty pair is unreachable (the typed-details check refuses an empty `Generation` first), so this is confined to direct callers of the exported helpers. Add one both-empty row to each table, or state the arm as entry-unreachable — but pick one and make the matrix say it.\n7|3. **P3-B — \"exactly 0700\" is pinned on the widened side only.** Narrowing `Perm() != 0o700` to `Perm()&0o077 != 0` (admitting owner-narrower modes such as 0600/0500) SURVIVED twice on both the create and verify entries; a pre-existing 0600 leaf returns nil under the mutant. This is not a confidentiality exposure, but `doc.go`, README, TRACEABILITY rows 1/4 and the `runtime.go` comment all say \"exact\"/\"exactly 0700\". Either pin the narrower side (a pre-existing 0600 leaf refuses `runtime mode` on both Ensure and Verify) or restate every one of those four sites as \"no group/world bits\" (mode ⊆ 0700). Prose and tests must agree; today they do not.\n8|4. **P3-C — the collision gate is byte equality, not path equality.** `checkAmbientDisjoint` (socket.go:103) compares strings, so an ambient value naming the derived socket through an unclean spelling (`dir/./ax-tmux.sock`, `dir//ax-tmux.sock`) or through a symlinked alias of the root walks past every member and `Acquire` spawns. The spec rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never selected from an ambient value — so this is a package-local defence-in-depth claim that outruns its tests. Either `filepath.Clean` both sides (symlink aliases remain an explicit bound) or state the byte-equality bound in TRACEABILITY. Row 23's \"colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member\" must end up true as written.\n9|5. **P3-D — the LOGBOOK carries a rev1 entry describing code that never reached trunk.** Lines 14-22 still claim `CheckLiveAttestation` \"admits only complete live sentinel+smoke\", \"all four ambient vectors\", \"Windows ownership is the creating-user ACL (tripwire-pinned)\", \"29 narrowing mutants\", \"54 of 54 rows\", \"87.5% statement coverage\" — all of it describes the rejected rev1 tree, and neither entry has landed. Fold the rev1 block into the rev2 block (keeping F1-F3 as the findings they are) or mark it superseded in place. Landing both blocks would record a design that was deleted before it ever existed on trunk.\n10|6. **P3-E — fail-closed error arms that are prose only.** `handleBoundToPath`'s two stat-failure arms (\"an unreadable root fails closed into the mismatch refusal\", runtime.go:127-139) flip to fail-open and survive, and `verifyOwnership`'s `!ok` arm (\"a stat without ownership metadata fails closed\", ownership_unix.go:29-34) is unstageable on unix. No test can stage a `Stat` failure on an open directory handle without a seam. State both as explicit BOUNDS (unmeasured error arms, no seam) or add the seam — and report them as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n11|7. **Three reviewer observations worth a sentence each in TRACEABILITY** (the reviewer did not file them as findings): the no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through `Dependencies.Spawn`, and a fallback through a direct `os/exec` call is excluded today only by the import census (no `os/exec` import in the package) — state that under B9; the mode gate reads permission bits only, so setgid/sticky on a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected, which matches the landed `hosttrust` custody precedent and is therefore the same bound, not a fork; and the derived socket path is not checked against the platform `sun_path` limit (104 bytes on macOS), which will surface in the lifecycle leaf's adapter — name TASK-260830-1c28dz as its owner.\n12|\n13|PROCESS. Keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED; exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept, and do NOT touch `internal/traceability` — the final leaf g0pcnt carries the registry. Run your own package tests, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` (the rev1 P1 — keep it green), and the harness BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once, reading the commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` in the candidate config. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, MANIFEST with no self-entry, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, zero `__pycache__`), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-35urbp --role developer` so revision 3 is constructed, and exit promptly. Report the ratio you MEASURE. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 3.\n14|REJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\n15|(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\n16|(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\n17|(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\n18|(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\n19|(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\n20|(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \"Composes X\", \"never admits what decoding refuses\", \"nothing re-implemented\", \"no cached sentinel can authorize\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\n21|Finally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.","final_result":true}}}
