{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":317,"recorded_at":1780531400000629,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c45b-7ca6-7641-a8f7-ecf46627425b"},"task_id":"01a0c45b-7ca6-7641-a8f7-ecf46627425b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c45b-7ca6-7641-a8f7-ecf46627425b","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TRACEABILITY — internal/tmuxserver (AX v0.7.0)\n2|\n3|Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 4.2 (tmux backend: dedicated -S\n4|server, no ambient/default discovery or reuse, credential-sensitive\n5|creation, background broker-or-refuse with typed capability_unavailable\n6|and no fallback to direct creation, launchctl managername as diagnostic\n7|hint only, cached observations never authorize resume), Section 4.C\n8|(operation vocabulary cited for the wrapper entrypoint shape only),\n9|Section 4.D (capability evidence cited landed), and Section 4.E\n10|(sensitive runtime state is owner-only and non-replicable). Story:\n11|production-tmux-backend (first leaf).\n12|\n13|Rule: every row names its production entry point. A row is driven only\n14|when the named committed test executes that entry. Prose in place of\n15|the ratio is not evidence. 55 of 55 AC rows driven (row 55 extends\n16|the rows 19-22 override class with the fifth ambient member,\n17|TMUX_TMPDIR); no row is a bound — the stated bounds below cover\n18|deliberately unclaimed surfaces, not undriven rows.\n19|\n20|No test in this package starts a tmux process: every broker, server,\n21|and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies, and the\n22|suite passes with no tmux installed. No row has a real-tmux witness;\n23|that is the determinism design, not a gap (bound B1).\n24|\n25|Attestation authority: the sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n26|verification, liveness, and expiry verdict is the landed\n27|internal/terminalbackend Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission,\n28|consumed here as an Admitted set composed only with the generation\n29|equality the wrapper owner (internal/axpane checkRealm) already\n30|enforces. This leaf decides membership plus generation binding and\n31|re-decides nothing the admission proves.\n32|\n33|## Runtime custody (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n34|\n35|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n36||---|--------|-----------|------|\n37|| 1 | Ensure creates the owner-only 0700 directory, explicitly under a restrictive umask | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirCreatesOwnerOnly, TestEnsureRuntimeDirEnforcesModeUnderRestrictiveUmask |\n38|| 2 | Re-ensure is idempotent and verifies mode | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent |\n39|| 3 | Compliant directory verifies | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirAdmitsCompliant |\n40|| 4 | Widened (0755) and narrower (0600/0500) modes refuse on ensure and verify, never silently repaired | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode, TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode |\n41|| 5 | Non-directory leaf refuses on commit and verify; the verify open carries no O_NONBLOCK by decision — FIFO refusal relies on O_DIRECTORY failing fast, pinned by the deadline test | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go), Acquire (acquire.go, background) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf (regular file, FIFO under deadline), TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf |\n42|| 6 | Symlink leaf refuses on commit and verify | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n43|| 7 | Foreign ownership refuses on ensure and verify | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (ownership_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership |\n44|| 8 | Handle/path mismatch refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesHandleMismatch |\n45|| 9 | Symlinked root refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkRoot |\n46|| 10 | Relative, empty, parent, and missing roots refuse | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadRoots (4 subtests) |\n47|| 11 | Empty, dot, parent, nested, absolute, and NUL names refuse | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadNames (6 subtests) |\n48|| 12 | Unknown platform refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadPlatform |\n49|| 13 | Verify refuses absence without creating | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence |\n50|| 14 | Linux and WSL2 share the unix custody discipline | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestLinuxAndWSL2ShareUnixCustody |\n51|| 15 | Windows platform refuses on every host; no tmux directory exists on Windows | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost, TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform |\n52|\n53|## Dedicated socket and ambient non-use (Section 4.2)\n54|\n55|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n56||---|--------|-----------|------|\n57|| 16 | Socket derives only from the runtime directory | SocketPath (socket.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir |\n58|| 17 | Resolution returns the derived socket under hostile ambient on all five members | ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n59|| 18 | Ambient observation records without using, including nil lookup | ObserveAmbient (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n60|| 19 | TMUX environment value as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable |\n61|| 20 | Inherited socket as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket |\n62|| 21 | Default path as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path |\n63|| 22 | Conventional name as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name |\n64|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member, byte-identical and unclean (`/./`, `//`) spellings alike | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpellings (2 subtests), TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpelling |\n65|| 55 | TMUX_TMPDIR value as override refuses through Acquire with no spawn and no directory | Acquire (acquire.go) via ResolveSocket (socket.go) | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir |\n66|\n67|## Background broker-or-refuse (Section 4.2)\n68|\n69|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n70||---|--------|-----------|------|\n71|| 24 | Authenticated same-user broker plus generation-bound attested server contacts on macOS, with no spawn and no argv | Acquire (acquire.go) via CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n72|| 25 | No broker returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/no_broker |\n73|| 26 | Foreign-user broker returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n74|| 27 | Unattested server returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unattested_server |\n75|| 28 | Stale-generation admission returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/generation-unbound_principal |\n76|| 29 | Linux miss also returns the typed capability_unavailable with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback |\n77|| 30 | Broker probe failure passes through as unknown, never unavailable, with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n78|| 31 | Creation gate refuses the background caller; the miss path enforces it by call | checkCreationAllowed via Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckCreationAllowedRefusesBackground, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable (kill path of N-creation-literal) |\n79|\n80|## Readiness non-authorization (Sections 4.2, 4.D)\n81|\n82|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n83||---|--------|-----------|------|\n84|| 32 | A stale admission replayed on a broker miss still returns the typed capability_unavailable: cached proof authorizes nothing | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission |\n85|| 33 | A stale admission fakes no running attested server on the foreground path | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission |\n86|| 34 | Bound admitted row admits | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedAdmitsBound |\n87|| 35 | Missing realm row refuses, including a decoy capability | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct (no admission rows, decoy capability only), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n88|| 36 | Wrong-generation admission refuses, including the both-empty pair | CheckServerAttested (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct (stale generation admission, both generations empty), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesWrongGenerationAdmission, TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/stale_server_admission |\n89|| 37 | Foreign-user broker principal refuses | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (no broker, foreign-user broker), TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n90|| 38 | Generation-unbound broker principal refuses, including the both-empty pair | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact (generation-unbound, empty and both-empty principal), TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/generation-unbound_principal |\n91|| 39 | Complete broker report admits | CheckBrokerContact (readiness.go) | TestCheckBrokerContactAdmitsLiveReport |\n92|\n93|## Foreground acquisition (Section 4.2)\n94|\n95|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n96||---|--------|-----------|------|\n97|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector and the ax pane tail | Acquire (acquire.go) via BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n98|| 41 | Running attested server attaches with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n99|| 42 | Running unattested server refuses with no spawn and no repair | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested |\n100|| 43 | Server probe failure passes through as unknown with no spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundProbeFailurePassesThrough |\n101|| 44 | Spawn failure reports with exactly one attempt and no fallback | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnFailureReportsWithoutFallback |\n102|| 45 | Malformed session refuses before any spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) via BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession |\n103|\n104|## Spawn argv (Sections 4.2, 4.C)\n105|\n106|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n107||---|--------|-----------|------|\n108|| 46 | Spawn vector is exactly tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n109|| 47 | All five ambient sockets refuse | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (5 subtests) |\n110|| 48 | Malformed sessions refuse the landed UUIDv7 wiring | BuildArgv (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesMalformedSession |\n111|\n112|## Input validation (Sections 4.2, 15.3)\n113|\n114|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n115||---|--------|-----------|------|\n116|| 49 | Unknown caller refuses | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesUnknownCaller |\n117|| 50 | Missing generation, broker state, and remediation each refuse | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesMissingRealmDetails (3 subtests) |\n118|| 51 | Missing dependencies refuse on every nil shape | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies, TestAcquireBackgroundNilBrokerWithSpawnRefuses, TestAcquireForegroundNilSpawnWithProbeRefuses |\n119|| 52 | Foreground acquisition ensures the runtime directory idempotently; background verifies without creating | Acquire (acquire.go) via EnsureRuntimeDir/VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently, TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating |\n120|\n121|## Crash and idempotency (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n122|\n123|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n124||---|--------|-----------|------|\n125|| 53 | Real SIGKILL between mkdir and fsync leaves a retry that converges to the one verified directory | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates |\n126|| 54 | Spawn-then-retry attaches to the one server with exactly one spawn | Acquire (acquire.go) | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry |\n127|\n128|## Mutation battery\n129|\n130|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`:\n131|46 narrowing rows KILLED, 1 supplementary additive row KILLED\n132|(D-background-fallback, labeled), 1 harmless control SURVIVED, on two\n133|full passes with identical verdicts and one raw log per plant per run.\n134|Row N-deps-foreground kills by panic: the admitted request calls the\n135|nil spawner and the panic fails the test. No token-preserving\n136|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text, and the\n137|harness executes the behavioral suite (bound B4). The rev2 reviewer's\n138|error-arm plant (stat-failure arms flipped to fail-open) is reported\n139|as an error-arm row under bound B15, never counted among the narrowing\n140|rows.\n141|\n142|## Stated bounds\n143|\n144|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n145|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n146|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n147|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n148|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n149|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n150|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n151|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n152|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n153|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n154|  panic kill.\n155|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n156|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n157|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n158|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n159|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n160|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n161|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n162|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n163|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n164|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n165|  conformance matrix only.\n166|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n167|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n168|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n169|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n170|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n171|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n172|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n173|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n174|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n175|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n176|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n177|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n178|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n179|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n180|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n181|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n182|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir;\n183|  through Acquire the directory always names a created directory.\n184|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n185|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n186|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n187|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n188|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n189|- B14 The battery assumes a non-root test user for exactly one row:\n190|  N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit chmod, so\n191|  under root it is equivalent to the original and survives. The\n192|  reviewer's same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n193|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n194|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n195|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n196|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n197|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. Reported\n198|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n199|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n200|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked alias of the\n201|  root walks past it (realpath equivalence is not applied). The spec\n202|  rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never selected from an\n203|  ambient value — so this bounds only the package-local\n204|  defense-in-depth claim.\n205|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n206|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n207|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n208|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n209|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n210|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n211|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep state root surfaces as\n212|  a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n213|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.","final_result":true}}}
