{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c703","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":476,"recorded_at":1780531400000947,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c45c-02db-79f1-a106-c93ed698c95c"},"task_id":"01a0c45c-02db-79f1-a106-c93ed698c95c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c45c-02db-79f1-a106-c93ed698c95c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp — review verdict, Change Request revision 3\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED** (routed `to-dev`). No P1. Three P2 classes, five P3. Every rev2\n4|finding (P2-A, P3-A..E, the three observations) is closed with driven evidence and stays closed;\n5|what remains is two spec-text divergences the earlier rounds did not examine (the socket path and\n6|the background return code for an absent runtime directory), one entry-level pin gap on the\n7|foreground \"running server never spawns\" rule, and prose/bound hygiene. The rework is enumerated\n8|at the end.\n9|\n10|- Reviewer run: RUN-260921-2369f7 (claude-opus-5 max), reviewing `CR-TASK-260830-35urbp-3`\n11|  revision 3 published by RUN-260921-ae96f3 (muse-spark max) after the rev2 rework brief.\n12|- Reviewed bytes: base `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2` (= `origin/main` after a fresh\n13|  `git fetch origin main`; `git diff --name-only 799c338 origin/main` empty — no trunk drift),\n14|  candidate tree `eb7b660c80a01f2ec0e2c4a728751d775fa263c2`, patch resource sha256\n15|  `c78d6635f5d77f995c418d3d450b5ee45e72340b7f4397cc2a40e18465a77132` (recomputed over the\n16|  materialized resource, equal to the CR record). The live Story worktree's uncommitted tree was\n17|  recomputed through a temporary index copy and equals the CR tree before and after this review.\n18|  Every measurement below was taken on three `git archive` copies of that tree\n19|  (`.temp/TASK-260830-35urbp/review-rev3/{candidate,mutant-copy,probe-copy}`), each re-hashed to\n20|  `eb7b660c` through a temporary index before and after use. The live worktree, its index, branch\n21|  and HEAD were not touched; no product edit, commit, checkpoint or integration was performed.\n22|  `git status` in the live worktree is unchanged (`M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n23|  `?? internal/tmuxserver/`).\n24|- Normative authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §4.2 (1403-1449), §4.3 (1458),\n25|  §4.4 (1468-1488), with §4.C/§4.D/§4.E as context, **and** §3.2 (765-813) where it names the\n26|  dedicated socket path and the runtime-directory custody rule this leaf implements. The task\n27|  record's v0.5.0 Scope is stale; the candidate cites the pinned file only (no `0.5.0` anywhere in\n28|  the package).\n29|- Note on the rev3 reviewer brief: its templated sentence \"revisions 1..2 carry no review verdict\"\n30|  is wrong for this task — rev1 (RUN-260921-0245e5) and rev2 (RUN-260921-5a9d4b) were both reviewed\n31|  and routed CHANGES REQUESTED. Rev3 was reviewed on its own merits AND against closure of every\n32|  rev2 finding.\n33|\n34|## What was reproduced (all on tree eb7b660c; PATH without any tmux binary, TMUX/TMUX_TMPDIR unset, no tmux process on the host; umask 022, uid 502)\n35|\n36|| Check | Result | Log (evidence archive) |\n37|| --- | --- | --- |\n38|| Configured suite, 30 commands read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (count 30, verified by read) | **30/30 green, every command rerun by this reviewer**: 1 gofmt (exact configured form in the live worktree, exit 0; plus `gofmt -l` over every tracked `.go` in the CR tree, empty), 2 build, 3 vet, 26 linux build, 27 windows build (`static-gates.log`); 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v`: 45/45 ok, 0 package FAIL, 0 top-level `--- FAIL`, 14 pre-existing SKIP outside this package, 21 indented `--- FAIL` lines are mutant-kill excerpts inside the passing resumesmoke `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled` (`cmd04-test-v.full.log`, 2m34s); 5 race: 45 ok, 0 `DATA RACE`, 6m43s in one call (`cmd05-race.log`); 6 cover: 45/45 ok, tmuxserver **91.6%** (`cmd06-cover.log`); 7-23 seventeen fuzz seeds exit 0, 24 tracecheck exit 0 (`clauses_discharged=70/574`), 25 cataloggen -check exit 0, 28 JSON parse over the CR tree's 141 tracked JSON files (0 bad), 30 `git diff --check` in the live worktree exit 0 (`cmd07-25-28-30.log`); 29 `task-board validate` exit 0 with the board's 180 pre-existing issues (`cmd29-validate.log`) | `logs/` |\n39|| Hosted-CI-shaped gate `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` (test files included) — the rev1 P1-A | **exit 0**; also `GOOS=windows go test -c ./internal/tmuxserver` exit 0, `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/tmuxserver` exit 0 | `static-gates.log` |\n40|| Package suite, tmux unresolvable | `go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1 -v`: 126 RUN / 126 PASS lines, **64 top-level PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP**. Determinism holds: no row's witness skips without tmux; no real-tmux witness exists (bound B1, honest) | `pkg-tests-notmux-v.log` |\n41|| Producer harness, two passes | **48/48 both passes** (46 narrowing + D-background-fallback KILLED exit 1, C-control SURVIVED exit 0); verdict lists identical to each other and to the producer's attached pass 1; mutant copy re-hashed to `eb7b660c` after each pass; zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` anywhere | `harness-pass1/`, `harness-pass2/`, `logs/harness-pass*-verdicts.log` |\n42|| Producer evidence archive | real gzip; MANIFEST 121 entries, no self-entry, **121/121 sha256 verify**; one raw log per plant per pass with `exit:` line; producer pass1 == pass2 | (checked in place) |\n43|| Reviewer battery, 11 rows × 2 passes | identical verdicts both passes; see §M | `reviewer-battery-pass1/`, `reviewer-battery-pass2/`, `reviewer_battery.py` |\n44|| Reviewer probes, 12 tests | all behave as described in §P | `logs/probes-rev3.log`, `zz_review_probe_test.go` |\n45|| Boundary / hygiene | `internal/traceability` untouched (`git diff --stat base tree -- internal/traceability` empty); no `0.5.0` citation; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or any copy; no `Getenv`/`Environ`/`os/exec` in any production file (socket.go imports `path/filepath` only); README section carries no `ax` command, `doctor` or capability claim; every one of the 58 test names in TRACEABILITY.md exists in the committed suite; row count 55 verified | `static-gates.log` |\n46|\n47|## Closure of the rev2 findings (verified by driving, not by reading the results table)\n48|\n49|| rev2 | Closed? | How verified |\n50|| --- | --- | --- |\n51|| P2-A verify-side non-directory leaf unpinned | **yes** | `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (regular 0700 file + FIFO under a 5s deadline) and `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` are committed; shipped row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` drops `O_DIRECTORY` on the verify `Openat` only and is KILLED in both of my harness passes with the predicted signature (err nil on both entries, 5s FIFO stall); row 5 names both entries; the no-`O_NONBLOCK` decision is stated in row 5 and in the test comment |\n52|| P3-A both-empty generation arms | **yes** | both-empty rows present in both tables; `N-realm-empty-want` and `N-broker-empty-generation` KILLED ×2 |\n53|| P3-B \"exactly 0700\" one-sided | **yes** | `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode` (0600, 0500; chmod-set fixtures) on both entries; `N-mode-narrower-create`/`-verify` KILLED ×2; prose kept and now true |\n54|| P3-C byte-equality collision | **yes** | `checkAmbientDisjoint` cleans the candidate; `/./` and `//` rows at `ResolveSocket` and through `Acquire`; `N-collision-unclean` KILLED ×2; symlink alias stated as B16 |\n55|| P3-D LOGBOOK rev1 block | **yes** | the rev1 block is a SUPERSEDED pointer; no landed entry describes `CheckLiveAttestation`, four vectors, the tripwire, 29 mutants, 54/54 or 87.5% |\n56|| P3-E prose-only stat arms | **yes** | B15 stated as error-arm rows |\n57|| Obs-1/2/3 | **yes** | B9 import-census sentence, B17 (hosttrust precedent), B18 (`sun_path`, owner 1c28dz) present |\n58|\n59|## P2 — must fix or record as a reviewed decision\n60|\n61|### P2-A. The derived path is not the path the specification mandates\n62|\n63|Pinned SPEC.v0.7.0.md §3.2 lines 806-813: \"On macOS the tmux backend MUST use a dedicated AX\n64|server selected by `tmux -S <runtime>/tmux/ax.sock`. The `<runtime>/tmux` parent MUST be\n65|AX-created, owned by the current user, mode 0700, and verified component-by-component without\n66|following a symlink.\" `<runtime>` is the Runtime IPC root of the §3.2 table (macOS: per-user\n67|temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), which the landed\n68|`internal/localstore` already resolves as `PathRuntime` (`paths.go:332-366`).\n69|\n70|The candidate hard-codes `RuntimeDirName = \"ax-tmux\"` (runtime.go:14) and\n71|`SocketName = \"ax-tmux.sock\"` (socket.go:10), so `SocketPath(filepath.Join(root, RuntimeDirName))`\n72|derives `<root>/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` (probe P01: `/runtime/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` against the\n73|spec's `/runtime/tmux/ax.sock`). `Request.Root` is documented as \"the AX state root\"\n74|(acquire.go:82-83, and \"under the AX state root\" at runtime.go:11-13), which names the durable\n75|`PathState` row of the §3.2 table rather than the Runtime IPC row the spec places the socket\n76|under — the socket \"is runtime IPC, never durable identity\" (SPEC 810) and a per-user temporary\n77|root is what makes the post-reboot absence case in P2-B the normal cold state.\n78|`TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` (tmuxserver_test.go:158-163) pins the literal\n79|`\"ax-tmux.sock\"`, so the suite currently protects the divergence instead of detecting it\n80|(\"check refusals against the normative source\"). No planning note, story record or spec text\n81|records `ax-tmux` as a decision; TRACEABILITY cites no §3.2 clause and states no bound.\n82|\n83|§3.2 is outside the sections the producer brief named as authority, which is why this was not\n84|raised in rev1/rev2; it is inside the spec text that governs exactly this leaf's deliverable, and\n85|AGENTS.md makes the whole pinned specification the authority for product behavior. Landing\n86|`ax-tmux.sock` now means the lifecycle leaf (1c28dz) builds its adapter on the wrong path and the\n87|final leaf's registry re-pin binds §3.2 to code that contradicts it.\n88|\n89|Fix (small): `RuntimeDirName = \"tmux\"`, `SocketName = \"ax.sock\"`; assert the literals `\"tmux\"`\n90|and `\"ax.sock\"` in `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` (and the joined spec form\n91|`<root>/tmux/ax.sock` once); document `Request.Root` as the Runtime IPC root\n92|(`localstore.PathRuntime`), not the state root; add a §3.2 row (path + custody clause) to\n93|TRACEABILITY and the conformance matrix; update README/doc.go. If the orchestrator decides the\n94|divergence is deliberate, that decision must be recorded as a stated bound naming the spec\n95|clause — today it is neither implemented nor bounded.\n96|\n97|### P2-B. A background caller with an absent runtime directory receives a custody code, not the `capability_unavailable` the spec mandates\n98|\n99|SPEC §4.2 lines 1419-1423: a background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon or restore worker \"MAY\n100|contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server; if neither\n101|exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT\n102|fall back to direct server creation.\"\n103|\n104|`acquireBackground` calls `VerifyRuntimeDir` before probing the broker (acquire.go:168) and\n105|returns its refusal verbatim. When the runtime directory does not exist — no server, therefore\n106|\"neither exists\" — the entry returns `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime containment` and never\n107|probes the broker (probe P02: `broker probed=false spawns=0`). With the Runtime IPC root being a\n108|per-user temporary directory on macOS, this is the ordinary post-reboot state of every background\n109|restore worker, not an edge. The committed test `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`\n110|(acquire_test.go:277-295) pins that local code, so the suite defends the divergence; README\n111|(§ \"Private tmux server management\") says background \"otherwise returns the typed\n112|`capability_unavailable` refusal\", which P02 disproves; TRACEABILITY row 13/52 state \"refuses\n113|absence\" without saying with which code.\n114|\n115|What the rev2 review verified — verify-never-create on the authorizing path, no durable write,\n116|no broker probe past a custody refusal — must stay. Only the classification of ABSENCE changes:\n117|a missing leaf is a readiness fact (nothing to contact) and must surface as the typed\n118|`capability_unavailable` with the request's realm/readiness details; a leaf that exists but fails\n119|mode/ownership/kind/symlink custody is unsafe (SPEC 810-812) and keeps the custody code. That\n120|requires the verify side to distinguish `ENOENT` from `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP`/other on its `Openat`\n121|(today all map to \"runtime containment\", see P3-B), so this finding and P3-B are one change.\n122|\n123|Fix: on the background path map \"leaf absent\" to `backgroundUnavailable(req, verr)` (no create,\n124|no probe needed — but probing the broker first and refusing the same way is also acceptable as\n125|long as no spawn and no directory write occur); keep every other custody refusal as is; update\n126|`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` to assert `capability_unavailable` + typed details\n127|+ no directory + zero spawns, add a sibling test that a widened/foreign/non-directory leaf on the\n128|background path still returns the custody code (the existing\n129|`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`/`...NonDirectoryLeaf` cover this), ship a\n130|narrowing row (e.g. the absence arm returning the custody code again) and fix README/row 13/52.\n131|\n132|### P2-C. The foreground \"running server → attach-or-refuse, never spawn\" rule is pinned at the entry only for running servers that carry some admission data\n133|\n134|`acquireForeground` (acquire.go:210-215) attaches or refuses when `report.Running`, and spawns\n135|otherwise. Every committed test that reports `Running: true`\n136|(`TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested`, `...RefusesRunningUnattested` (decoy row),\n137|`...RefusesWrongGenerationAdmission`, `TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry`) carries\n138|a non-empty `Admitted.Capabilities` AND a non-empty `RawGeneration`. The realistic post-spawn\n139|state — the server runs, no evidence has been reconciled yet, `RealmAdmission{}` — is driven only\n140|at the helper (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct/no_admission_rows`), never\n141|through `Acquire` (rejection pattern b). Two reviewer narrowings on the entry SURVIVED the\n142|committed suite in both passes and are KILLED by my probes:\n143|\n144|- `R01-running-empty-admission`: `if report.Running` → `if report.Running &&\n145|  len(report.Admission.Admitted.Capabilities) > 0` — a running server with zero admission rows is\n146|  treated as absent and `Acquire` spawns a second `new-session` into it (P07 baseline: production\n147|  refuses `tmux_readiness_not_authorizing at server attestation`, spawn 0).\n148|- `R02-running-empty-generation`: `if report.Running` → `if report.Running &&\n149|  report.Admission.RawGeneration != \"\"` — same effect for a running server whose admission carries\n150|  no generation (P08 baseline: production refuses `server generation`, spawn 0).\n151|\n152|Production is correct today (P07/P08 pass on the candidate). The DoD line \"refusing behavior\n153|covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production\n154|call site named\" is not met for these two members at the entry the matrix names for rows 41/42.\n155|Fix: commit the two entry-level tests (P07/P08 are templates: `Running: true` with\n156|`RealmAdmission{}` → `server attestation`, spawn 0; `Running: true` with the realm row and empty\n157|`RawGeneration` → `server generation`, spawn 0), ship `N-running-empty-admission` and\n158|`N-running-empty-generation` as the R01/R02 narrowings, and name them under rows 41/42.\n159|\n160|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n161|\n162|- **P3-A. The TMUX-env collision member is measured on a shape tmux never produces.** tmux sets\n163|  `TMUX=<socket>,<pid>,<index>`; the hostile fixture uses exactly that encoding\n164|  (`/tmp/tmux-501/default,12345,0`), but the collision rows feed the bare derived path into\n165|  `TMUXEnv`. A `TMUX` value naming the derived socket in the real encoding walks past\n166|  `checkAmbientDisjoint` and `Acquire` spawns (probe P06: `via=spawned spawns=1`). Row 23's\n167|  \"colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member\" therefore holds for the TMUX member\n168|  only in an unrealistic spelling. Either compare the socket component (the substring before the\n169|  first comma) for the `TMUXEnv` member with a test in the real encoding, or state the bound\n170|  under B16 and reword row 23. Spec rule unaffected (the socket is derived, never selected).\n171|- **P3-B. Absence and a failure to read are the same fact on the verify side.** `verifyRuntimeDir`\n172|  maps `ENOENT` (absent leaf), `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP` (unsafe leaf) and a missing root all to\n173|  `runtime containment` (runtime_unix.go:97-108), while the commit side maps a missing root to\n174|  `tmux_invalid_arguments at runtime root` (runtime_unix.go:28-29). Probe P03: verify-absent-leaf\n175|  == verify-symlink-leaf byte for byte; missing root differs across Ensure/Verify. Distinguish\n176|  absence (its own detail, consumed by P2-B) and align the missing-root mapping across the two\n177|  entries (rows 10/13 then name the same code).\n178|- **P3-C. Root custody is not gated and not bounded.** A world-writable (0777) root admits the\n179|  leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir`, `VerifyRuntimeDir` and the background broker path (probes P04, P11).\n180|  SPEC 810-812 requires rejecting \"a socket path, parent, or ancestor whose ... ownership, or\n181|  permissions are unsafe\" before bind/connect. B11 covers symlinked intermediates only; nothing\n182|  states who verifies the root's own mode/ownership (the `localstore` layout owner, the lifecycle\n183|  bind step, or this leaf). Likewise \"AX-created\" (SPEC 808) is not distinguishable after the\n184|  fact — any same-user 0700 directory under any admitted `Name` is accepted as the runtime\n185|  directory (probe P05 admits a pre-existing `tmux-501`). State both as explicit bounds with the\n186|  named owner, or gate the root's mode/ownership on the pinned root handle.\n187|- **P3-D. Prose that outruns the code in socket.go.** Lines 28-31 say both environment names\n188|  \"are validated by the landed environment-name grammar at the observation boundary, so a\n189|  misspelled variable cannot smuggle an ambient value past the non-use proof\" — that arm was\n190|  deleted in rev2 (no `environ`/`secprim` import remains; probe P09 shows the lookup is called\n191|  with the two constants and nothing is validated). `ObserveAmbient`'s `error` return is always\n192|  nil since that deletion. Fix the comment and drop the vestigial return (or state what the\n193|  return is for). Rejection pattern (f).\n194|- **P3-E. Two refusal arms are pinned by detail in prose only.** `R04-mkdirat-eacces-as-exist`\n195|  (a permission failure at `Mkdirat` treated as `EEXIST`) SURVIVED ×2: no committed test stages a\n196|  read-only root, so the `runtime commit` detail at runtime_unix.go:41 is unmeasured (my P12 kills\n197|  it: the refusal reroutes to `runtime containment` — still fail-closed, hence P3). `R07`\n198|  (a two-space override admitted and ignored) SURVIVED ×2 — the override gate is pinned on the\n199|  five hostile literals only; a whitespace-only override row closes it. Add the two rows or\n200|  report the arms as bounds; neither admits an unsafe state.\n201|\n202|## Observations (not findings; a sentence each in TRACEABILITY if the producer agrees)\n203|\n204|- \"No broker\" is modelled as the zero `BrokerReport{}`, whose `Principal.UID` is 0 — a real UID.\n205|  Under a root process the same-user arm passes for an absent broker and refusal comes from the\n206|  generation arm (`R21-broker-uid-zero` is KILLED only by the helper-level detail pin; through\n207|  `Acquire` both arms collapse into the same typed unavailable). Worth stating next to B14, or\n208|  giving the report an explicit presence fact.\n209|- `Hooks.AfterMkdir` also fires on the `EEXIST` path (created == false); harmless for the crash\n210|  test, but the name promises a mkdir that did not happen.\n211|- `R03-guard-resolve-failopen` (the `guard.Resolve` refusal arm at runtime.go:94-97 flipped to\n212|  fail-open) SURVIVED ×2 — the name grammar refuses every input before the guard can; report it as\n213|  an unreachable/error arm alongside B15 rather than as a gate.\n214|- On the broker path the outcome carries the derived socket while `BrokerReport` carries no\n215|  socket; the binding between \"its attested AX tmux server\" and the derived path is the generation\n216|  equality only. Acceptable under the spec's generation model; worth one sentence under B13.\n217|\n218|## §M — reviewer battery (11 rows, two passes, `reviewer_battery.py` in the evidence archive)\n219|\n220|Every row: anchor count verified (all 11 applied, none NOT_APPLIED), plant applied to the mutant\n221|copy, the committed suite run as shipped (full package, no `-run` mask), exit + raw output logged,\n222|file restored from a byte copy and re-compared, tree re-hashed to `eb7b660c` after each pass.\n223|Rows predicted SURVIVED were additionally run with `zz_review_probe_test.go` present and the\n224|named killer selected (`*.with-probe.log`).\n225|\n226|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer |\n227|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n228|| R01-running-empty-admission | narrowing | `if report.Running` gains `&& len(Admitted.Capabilities) > 0` (acquire.go:210) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P07 |\n229|| R02-running-empty-generation | narrowing | `if report.Running` gains `&& RawGeneration != \"\"` (acquire.go:210) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P08 |\n230|| R03-guard-resolve-failopen | error-arm | `guard.Resolve` refusal → fail-open join (runtime.go:94-97) | **SURVIVED** | (unreachable through the name grammar) | — |\n231|| R04-mkdirat-eacces-as-exist | narrowing | `!EEXIST` gains `&& !EACCES` (runtime_unix.go:40) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED (reroute to `runtime containment`) | P12 |\n232|| R07-override-two-spaces | narrowing | `override != \"\"` gains `&& override != \"  \"` (socket.go:81) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P10 |\n233|| R15-argv-detached-flag | positive-pin | drop `\"-d\"` from the spawn vector (argv.go:28) | KILLED | — | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n234|| R17-realm-capability-swap | constant-swap | `realmCapability` → `\"headless_creation\"` (acquire.go:47) | KILLED | — | literal detail/fixture assertions (rejection pattern a holds) |\n235|| R18-via-literal-swap | constant-swap | `ViaAttached` → `\"attached\"` (acquire.go:35) | KILLED | — | literal outcome assertions |\n236|| R21-broker-uid-zero | narrowing | UID arm admits principal UID 0 (readiness.go:80) | KILLED | — | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact/no_broker (helper-level detail) |\n237|| R26-background-absent-ensures | additive | background creates the directory when verify fails (acquire.go:168) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating |\n238|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in acquire.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n239|\n240|Denominator: 11 applied rows = 5 narrowing + 1 additive + 1 error-arm + 1 positive-pin + 2\n241|constant-swap + 1 control. Of the 5 narrowings, 1 KILLED by the committed suite (R21), 4 SURVIVED\n242|and each is proven real by a probe kill (R01, R02, R04, R07). Every KILLED row was killed by\n243|exactly the test named above (kill lines in the raw logs).\n244|\n245|## §P — reviewer probes (12, `logs/probes-rev3.log`)\n246|\n247|P01 derived `/runtime/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` vs spec `/runtime/tmux/ax.sock` (P2-A); P02 background\n248|+ absent runtime dir → `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime containment`, broker not probed, 0\n249|spawns (P2-B); P03 verify absent leaf == verify symlink leaf; missing root differs across\n250|Ensure/Verify (P3-B); P04 0777 root admitted on Ensure and Verify (P3-C); P05 pre-existing\n251|non-AX `tmux-501` directory admitted (P3-C bound); P06 `TMUX=<derived>,12345,0` → spawned (P3-A);\n252|P07 running + `RealmAdmission{}` refuses `server attestation`, spawn 0 (baseline for R01); P08\n253|running + realm row + empty `RawGeneration` refuses `server generation`, spawn 0 (baseline for\n254|R02); P09 `ObserveAmbient` validates nothing (P3-D); P10 two-space override refuses (baseline for\n255|R07); P11 background broker path admits under a 0777 root (P3-C); P12 read-only root refuses\n256|`runtime commit` (baseline for R04).\n257|\n258|## What held under attack (keep)\n259|\n260|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members through `Acquire` with\n261|  no spawn and no directory; byte-identical and cleaned collisions refused on all five; argv gate\n262|  refuses all five; `Acquire` never reads the environment or execs.\n263|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6 and the five\n264|  typed details asserted as literals for every miss with an existing directory; no fallback along\n265|  the caller (N-creation-literal), platform (Linux miss), spawner (D-background-fallback) and\n266|  directory-write (R26, R25/R07 of rev2) axes; same-user generation-bound broker principal at the\n267|  entry.\n268|- Attestation: landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` consumed through `Has` composed with the\n269|  generation equality axpane enforces; stale, decoy and both-empty shapes refuse; the rev1 fork\n270|  stays deleted; constant swaps (R17/R18) redden literal assertions.\n271|- Custody: FIFO leaf refuses on both entries without blocking (5s deadline pinned), symlink leaf /\n272|  root, widened and narrower modes, foreign UID and handle mismatch refuse on both entries; the\n273|  explicit `Fchmod` is load-bearing under umask 0177; the real-SIGKILL crash test converges.\n274|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable; no real-tmux witness (B1).\n275|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim; no\n276|  trunk drift; producer evidence archive complete and digest-verified.\n277|\n278|## Coverage ratio measured against the 55-row table\n279|\n280|**55 of 55 rows are driven as their statements are written**; the ratio is not inflated. The gaps\n281|above sit beside the statements: row 16 pins a socket literal the spec contradicts (P2-A), rows\n282|13/52 state \"refuses absence\" without the code the spec mandates (P2-B), rows 41/42 are driven for\n283|running servers with admission data only (P2-C), row 23 holds for the TMUX member only in a\n284|non-tmux spelling (P3-A), and no row cites §3.2 (P2-A, P3-C).\n285|\n286|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n287|\n288|1. **P2-A**: `RuntimeDirName = \"tmux\"`, `SocketName = \"ax.sock\"`; assert the literals in\n289|   `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir`; document `Request.Root` as the Runtime IPC root\n290|   (`localstore.PathRuntime`); add a §3.2 row (SPEC 806-813) to TRACEABILITY and the matrix;\n291|   update