vectors, the tripwire, 29 mutants, 54/54 or 87.5% |\n56|| P3-E prose-only stat arms | **yes** | B15 stated as error-arm rows |\n57|| Obs-1/2/3 | **yes** | B9 import-census sentence, B17 (hosttrust precedent), B18 (`sun_path`, owner 1c28dz) present |\n58|\n59|## P2 — must fix or record as a reviewed decision\n60|\n61|### P2-A. The derived path is not the path the specification mandates\n62|\n63|Pinned SPEC.v0.7.0.md §3.2 lines 806-813: \"On macOS the tmux backend MUST use a dedicated AX\n64|server selected by `tmux -S <runtime>/tmux/ax.sock`. The `<runtime>/tmux` parent MUST be\n65|AX-created, owned by the current user, mode 0700, and verified component-by-component without\n66|following a symlink.\" `<runtime>` is the Runtime IPC root of the §3.2 table (macOS: per-user\n67|temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), which the landed\n68|`internal/localstore` already resolves as `PathRuntime` (`paths.go:332-366`).\n69|\n70|The candidate hard-codes `RuntimeDirName = \"ax-tmux\"` (runtime.go:14) and\n71|`SocketName = \"ax-tmux.sock\"` (socket.go:10), so `SocketPath(filepath.Join(root, RuntimeDirName))`\n72|derives `<root>/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` (probe P01: `/runtime/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` against the\n73|spec's `/runtime/tmux/ax.sock`). `Request.Root` is documented as \"the AX state root\"\n74|(acquire.go:82-83, and \"under the AX state root\" at runtime.go:11-13), which names the durable\n75|`PathState` row of the §3.2 table rather than the Runtime IPC row the spec places the socket\n76|under — the socket \"is runtime IPC, never durable identity\" (SPEC 810) and a per-user temporary\n77|root is what makes the post-reboot absence case in P2-B the normal cold state.\n78|`TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` (tmuxserver_test.go:158-163) pins the literal\n79|`\"ax-tmux.sock\"`, so the suite currently protects the divergence instead of detecting it\n80|(\"check refusals against the normative source\"). No planning note, story record or spec text\n81|records `ax-tmux` as a decision; TRACEABILITY cites no §3.2 clause and states no bound.\n82|\n83|§3.2 is outside the sections the producer brief named as authority, which is why this was not\n84|raised in rev1/rev2; it is inside the spec text that governs exactly this leaf's deliverable, and\n85|AGENTS.md makes the whole pinned specification the authority for product behavior. Landing\n86|`ax-tmux.sock` now means the lifecycle leaf (1c28dz) builds its adapter on the wrong path and the\n87|final leaf's registry re-pin binds §3.2 to code that contradicts it.\n88|\n89|Fix (small): `RuntimeDirName = \"tmux\"`, `SocketName = \"ax.sock\"`; assert the literals `\"tmux\"`\n90|and `\"ax.sock\"` in `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` (and the joined spec form\n91|`<root>/tmux/ax.sock` once); document `Request.Root` as the Runtime IPC root\n92|(`localstore.PathRuntime`), not the state root; add a §3.2 row (path + custody clause) to\n93|TRACEABILITY and the conformance matrix; update README/doc.go. If the orchestrator decides the\n94|divergence is deliberate, that decision must be recorded as a stated bound naming the spec\n95|clause — today it is neither implemented nor bounded.\n96|\n97|### P2-B. A background caller with an absent runtime directory receives a custody code, not the `capability_unavailable` the spec mandates\n98|\n99|SPEC §4.2 lines 1419-1423: a background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon or restore worker \"MAY\n100|contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server; if neither\n101|exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT\n102|fall back to direct server creation.\"\n103|\n104|`acquireBackground` calls `VerifyRuntimeDir` before probing the broker (acquire.go:168) and\n105|returns its refusal verbatim. When the runtime directory does not exist — no server, therefore\n106|\"neither exists\" — the entry returns `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime containment` and never\n107|probes the broker (probe P02: `broker probed=false spawns=0`). With the Runtime IPC root being a\n108|per-user temporary directory on macOS, this is the ordinary post-reboot state of every background\n109|restore worker, not an edge. The committed test `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`\n110|(acquire_test.go:277-295) pins that local code, so the suite defends the divergence; README\n111|(§ \"Private tmux server management\") says background \"otherwise returns the typed\n112|`capability_unavailable` refusal\", which P02 disproves; TRACEABILITY row 13/52 state \"refuses\n113|absence\" without saying with which code.\n114|\n115|What the rev2 review verified — verify-never-create on the authorizing path, no durable write,\n116|no broker probe past a custody refusal — must stay. Only the classification of ABSENCE changes:\n117|a missing leaf is a readiness fact (nothing to contact) and must surface as the typed\n118|`capability_unavailable` with the request's realm/readiness details; a leaf that exists but fails\n119|mode/ownership/kind/symlink custody is unsafe (SPEC 810-812) and keeps the custody code. That\n120|requires the verify side to distinguish `ENOENT` from `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP`/other on its `Openat`\n121|(today all map to \"runtime containment\", see P3-B), so this finding and P3-B are one change.\n122|\n123|Fix: on the background path map \"leaf absent\" to `backgroundUnavailable(req, verr)` (no create,\n124|no probe needed — but probing the broker first and refusing the same way is also acceptable as\n125|long as no spawn and no directory write occur); keep every other custody refusal as is; update\n126|`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` to assert `capability_unavailable` + typed details\n127|+ no directory + zero spawns, add a sibling test that a widened/foreign/non-directory leaf on the\n128|background path still returns the custody code (the existing\n129|`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`/`...NonDirectoryLeaf` cover this), ship a\n130|narrowing row (e.g. the absence arm returning the custody code again) and fix README/row 13/52.\n131|\n132|### P2-C. The foreground \"running server → attach-or-refuse, never spawn\" rule is pinned at the entry only for running servers that carry some admission data\n133|\n134|`acquireForeground` (acquire.go:210-215) attaches or refuses when `report.Running`, and spawns\n135|otherwise. Every committed test that reports `Running: true`\n136|(`TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested`, `...RefusesRunningUnattested` (decoy row),\n137|`...RefusesWrongGenerationAdmission`, `TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry`) carries\n138|a non-empty `Admitted.Capabilities` AND a non-empty `RawGeneration`. The realistic post-spawn\n139|state — the server runs, no evidence has been reconciled yet, `RealmAdmission{}` — is driven only\n140|at the helper (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct/no_admission_rows`), never\n141|through `Acquire` (rejection pattern b). Two reviewer narrowings on the entry SURVIVED the\n142|committed suite in both passes and are KILLED by my probes:\n143|\n144|- `R01-running-empty-admission`: `if report.Running` → `if report.Running &&\n145|  len(report.Admission.Admitted.Capabilities) > 0` — a running server with zero admission rows is\n146|  treated as absent and `Acquire` spawns a second `new-session` into it (P07 baseline: production\n147|  refuses `tmux_readiness_not_authorizing at server attestation`, spawn 0).\n148|- `R02-running-empty-generation`: `if report.Running` → `if report.Running &&\n149|  report.Admission.RawGeneration != \"\"` — same effect for a running server whose admission carries\n150|  no generation (P08 baseline: production refuses `server generation`, spawn 0).\n151|\n152|Production is correct today (P07/P08 pass on the candidate). The DoD line \"refusing behavior\n153|covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production\n154|call site named\" is not met for these two members at the entry the matrix names for rows 41/42.\n155|Fix: commit the two entry-level tests (P07/P08 are templates: `Running: true` with\n156|`RealmAdmission{}` → `server attestation`, spawn 0; `Running: true` with the realm row and empty\n157|`RawGeneration` → `server generation`, spawn 0), ship `N-running-empty-admission` and\n158|`N-running-empty-generation` as the R01/R02 narrowings, and name them under rows 41/42.\n159|\n160|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n161|\n162|- **P3-A. The TMUX-env collision member is measured on a shape tmux never produces.** tmux sets\n163|  `TMUX=<socket>,<pid>,<index>`; the hostile fixture uses exactly that encoding\n164|  (`/tmp/tmux-501/default,12345,0`), but the collision rows feed the bare derived path into\n165|  `TMUXEnv`. A `TMUX` value naming the derived socket in the real encoding walks past\n166|  `checkAmbientDisjoint` and `Acquire` spawns (probe P06: `via=spawned spawns=1`). Row 23's\n167|  \"colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member\" therefore holds for the TMUX member\n168|  only in an unrealistic spelling. Either compare the socket component (the substring before the\n169|  first comma) for the `TMUXEnv` member with a test in the real encoding, or state the bound\n170|  under B16 and reword row 23. Spec rule unaffected (the socket is derived, never selected).\n171|- **P3-B. Absence and a failure to read are the same fact on the verify side.** `verifyRuntimeDir`\n172|  maps `ENOENT` (absent leaf), `ENOTDIR`/`ELOOP` (unsafe leaf) and a missing root all to\n173|  `runtime containment` (runtime_unix.go:97-108), while the commit side maps a missing root to\n174|  `tmux_invalid_arguments at runtime root` (runtime_unix.go:28-29). Probe P03: verify-absent-leaf\n175|  == verify-symlink-leaf byte for byte; missing root differs across Ensure/Verify. Distinguish\n176|  absence (its own detail, consumed by P2-B) and align the missing-root mapping across the two\n177|  entries (rows 10/13 then