e_test.go` present and the\n224|named killer selected (`*.with-probe.log`).\n225|\n226|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer |\n227|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n228|| R01-running-empty-admission | narrowing | `if report.Running` gains `&& len(Admitted.Capabilities) > 0` (acquire.go:210) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P07 |\n229|| R02-running-empty-generation | narrowing | `if report.Running` gains `&& RawGeneration != \"\"` (acquire.go:210) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P08 |\n230|| R03-guard-resolve-failopen | error-arm | `guard.Resolve` refusal → fail-open join (runtime.go:94-97) | **SURVIVED** | (unreachable through the name grammar) | — |\n231|| R04-mkdirat-eacces-as-exist | narrowing | `!EEXIST` gains `&& !EACCES` (runtime_unix.go:40) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED (reroute to `runtime containment`) | P12 |\n232|| R07-override-two-spaces | narrowing | `override != \"\"` gains `&& override != \"  \"` (socket.go:81) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | P10 |\n233|| R15-argv-detached-flag | positive-pin | drop `\"-d\"` from the spawn vector (argv.go:28) | KILLED | — | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n234|| R17-realm-capability-swap | constant-swap | `realmCapability` → `\"headless_creation\"` (acquire.go:47) | KILLED | — | literal detail/fixture assertions (rejection pattern a holds) |\n235|| R18-via-literal-swap | constant-swap | `ViaAttached` → `\"attached\"` (acquire.go:35) | KILLED | — | literal outcome assertions |\n236|| R21-broker-uid-zero | narrowing | UID arm admits principal UID 0 (readiness.go:80) | KILLED | — | TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact/no_broker (helper-level detail) |\n237|| R26-background-absent-ensures | additive | background creates the directory when verify fails (acquire.go:168) | KILLED | — | TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating |\n238|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in acquire.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n239|\n240|Denominator: 11 applied rows = 5 narrowing + 1 additive + 1 error-arm + 1 positive-pin + 2\n241|constant-swap + 1 control. Of the 5 narrowings, 1 KILLED by the committed suite (R21), 4 SURVIVED\n242|and each is proven real by a probe kill (R01, R02, R04, R07). Every KILLED row was killed by\n243|exactly the test named above (kill lines in the raw logs).\n244|\n245|## §P — reviewer probes (12, `logs/probes-rev3.log`)\n246|\n247|P01 derived `/runtime/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` vs spec `/runtime/tmux/ax.sock` (P2-A); P02 background\n248|+ absent runtime dir → `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime containment`, broker not probed, 0\n249|spawns (P2-B); P03 verify absent leaf == verify symlink leaf; missing root differs across\n250|Ensure/Verify (P3-B); P04 0777 root admitted on Ensure and Verify (P3-C); P05 pre-existing\n251|non-AX `tmux-501` directory admitted (P3-C bound); P06 `TMUX=<derived>,12345,0` → spawned (P3-A);\n252|P07 running + `RealmAdmission{}` refuses `server attestation`, spawn 0 (baseline for R01); P08\n253|running + realm row + empty `RawGeneration` refuses `server generation`, spawn 0 (baseline for\n254|R02); P09 `ObserveAmbient` validates nothing (P3-D); P10 two-space override refuses (baseline for\n255|R07); P11 background broker path admits under a 0777 root (P3-C); P12 read-only root refuses\n256|`runtime commit` (baseline for R04).\n257|\n258|## What held under attack (keep)\n259|\n260|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members through `Acquire` with\n261|  no spawn and no directory; byte-identical and cleaned collisions refused on all five; argv gate\n262|  refuses all five; `Acquire` never reads the environment or execs.\n263|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6 and the five\n264|  typed details asserted as literals for every miss with an existing directory; no fallback along\n265|  the caller (N-creation-literal), platform (Linux miss), spawner (D-background-fallback) and\n266|  directory-write (R26, R25/R07 of rev2) axes; same-user generation-bound broker principal at the\n267|  entry.\n268|- Attestation: landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` consumed through `Has` composed with the\n269|  generation equality axpane enforces; stale, decoy and both-empty shapes refuse; the rev1 fork\n270|  stays deleted; constant swaps (R17/R18) redden literal assertions.\n271|- Custody: FIFO leaf refuses on both entries without blocking (5s deadline pinned), symlink leaf /\n272|  root, widened and narrower modes, foreign UID and handle mismatch refuse on both entries; the\n273|  explicit `Fchmod` is load-bearing under umask 0177; the real-SIGKILL crash test converges.\n274|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable; no real-tmux witness (B1).\n275|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim; no\n276|  trunk drift; producer evidence archive complete and digest-verified.\n277|\n278|## Coverage ratio measured against the 55-row table\n279|\n280|**55 of 55 rows are driven as their statements are written**; the ratio is not inflated. The gaps\n281|above sit beside the statements: row 16 pins a socket literal the spec contradicts (P2-A), rows\n282|13/52 state \"refuses absence\" without the code the spec mandates (P2-B), rows 41/42 are driven for\n283|running servers with admission data only (P2-C), row 23 holds for the TMUX member only in a\n284|non-tmux spelling (P3-A), and no row cites §3.2 (P2-A, P3-C).\n285|\n286|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n287|\n288|1. **P2-A**: `RuntimeDirName = \"tmux\"`, `SocketName = \"ax.sock\"`; assert the literals in\n289|   `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir`; document `Request.Root` as the Runtime IPC root\n290|   (`localstore.PathRuntime`); add a §3.2 row (SPEC 806-813) to TRACEABILITY and the matrix;\n291|   update README/doc.go/LOGBOOK — or record the divergence as an explicit reviewed bound naming\n292|   the clause (orchestrator decision).\n293|2. **P2-B + P3-B**: distinguish `ENOENT` on the verify `Openat` (and align the missing-root code\n294|   with the commit side); on the background path return the typed `capability_unavailable` for an\n295|   absent leaf (no create, no spawn), keep the custody code for an unsafe leaf; rewrite\n296|   `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` to assert the typed refusal + no directory + zero\n297|   spawns; ship a narrowing row; fix README \"otherwise returns\" and rows 13/52.\n298|3. **P2-C**: commit the two entry-level tests (running + `RealmAdmission{}` → `server attestation`;\n299|   running + realm row + empty `RawGeneration` → `server generation`; spawn 0 in both) and ship\n300|   `N-running-empty-admission` / `N-running-empty-generation`; name them under rows 41/42.\n301|4. **P3-A**: compare the socket component of the `TMUXEnv` member (split at the first comma) with\n302|   a real-encoding collision test, or state the bound and reword row 23.\n303|5. **P3-C**: state root custody and \"AX-created\" as bounds with named owners, or gate the root's\n304|   mode/ownership on the pinned handle.\n305|6. **P3-D**: fix socket.go:28-31 and the vestigial `ObserveAmbient` error return.\n306|7. **P3-E**: add a read-only-root row (`runtime commit`) and a whitespace-override row, or report\n307|   both arms as bounds.\n308|8. Rerun the package suite (tmux hidden), `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, the harness\n309|   twice, and the 30-command suite; refresh results/matrix/archive; hand off as revision 4.\n310|   Everything in \"What held under attack\" needs no change — do not re-litigate it.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
