{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c739","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":503,"recorded_at":1780531400001001,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"call_id":"call_01a0c45c1ec07730a98ae1b60c4d6122","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp results — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev3)\n2|\n3|Rework of revision 2 after review-verdict-rev2 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no\n4|P1, one P2 class, five P3). First leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i\n5|(production-tmux-backend, EPIC M1). The reviewer states every rev1\n6|P1/P2/P3 finding is closed with driven evidence; this revision keeps\n7|all of that and changes nothing the verdict grades closed.\n8|\n9|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch\n10|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` atop trunk `799c338` (trunk\n11|unmoved since rev2; no refresh, no rebase, no commit, no merge by this\n12|run). `git status` shows only `internal/tmuxserver/`, `README.md`,\n13|`LOGBOOK.md`.\n14|\n15|Normative source: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n16|§4.2 tmux backend (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220),\n17|and §4.E (1309) as context, plus §4.3 (1458) and §4.4 for the\n18|Windows and broker rules. All clause citations name the pinned file,\n19|never the network, never v0.5.0.\n20|\n21|## Finding-by-finding table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\n22|\n23|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n24||---|---|---|---|\n25|| P2-A verify-side non-directory leaf unpinned (background path admits a 0700 file, FIFO blocks 5s under the one-flag narrowing) | Committed `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (regular 0700 file + FIFO under a 5s deadline) and `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (regular-file shape through the background entry, asserting no broker probe); shipped row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` (drops `O_DIRECTORY` on the verify `Openat` only); row 5 names both entries. Deliberate gate decision: the verify `Openat` carries no `O_NONBLOCK` — FIFO refusal relies on `O_DIRECTORY` failing fast with ENOTDIR, symmetric with the commit side, pinned by the deadline test and stated in TRACEABILITY row 5 | `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf/regular_file` (err nil under the mutant), `.../fifo_without_blocking` (BLOCKED 5s under the mutant), `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (err nil under the mutant) | `harness-pass1/N-containment-odirectory-verify.log`, `harness-pass2/N-containment-odirectory-verify.log`, `pkg-tests-v.log` |\n26|| P3-A both-empty generation arms unmeasured on two exported entries | One both-empty row in each table (`TestCheckServerAttestedRefusesEachMissingConjunct/both_generations_empty`, `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact/both_generations_empty` with a new `want` column); shipped rows `N-realm-empty-want` and `N-broker-empty-generation` (each drops exactly the `== \"\"` disjunct) | The both-empty rows (admission / reroute to the server-generation detail under the mutants) | `harness-pass1/N-realm-empty-want.log`, `harness-pass1/N-broker-empty-generation.log` (+ pass 2) |\n27|| P3-B \"exactly 0700\" pinned on the widened side only | Pinned the narrower side: pre-existing 0600/0500 leaves refuse `runtime mode` on both Ensure and Verify (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode`, chmod-set fixtures exact under any umask); shipped rows `N-mode-narrower-create` / `N-mode-narrower-verify` (each admits exactly 0600 on one arm). Prose (\"exact(ly) 0700\" in doc-adjacent comments, README, TRACEABILITY rows 1/4, runtime.go) kept, now true as written | `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode` (Ensure leg under the create mutant, Verify leg under the verify mutant) | `harness-pass1/N-mode-narrower-create.log`, `harness-pass1/N-mode-narrower-verify.log` (+ pass 2) |\n28|| P3-C collision gate is byte equality, not path equality | `checkAmbientDisjoint` compares `filepath.Clean(candidate)` against the derived socket; tests for `/./` and `//` spellings at `ResolveSocket` and through `Acquire`; shipped row `N-collision-unclean` (drops `Clean`, byte-identical collisions still refuse); symlink aliases stay an explicit bound (B16); the five existing N-collision rows re-anchored to the new line | `TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpellings`, `TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpelling` | `harness-pass1/N-collision-unclean.log` (+ pass 2), re-anchored `N-collision-*.log` |\n29|| P3-D LOGBOOK rev1 block describes code that never reached trunk | Rev1 block folded into the rev2 block: F1-F3 preserved as a findings bullet in the rev2 entry, the rev1 DELIVERED/mutation/AC/bounds bullets deleted and replaced with a SUPERSEDED pointer; rev3 entry added newest-first | — (prose hygiene; no behavior) | `LOGBOOK.md` diff |\n30|| P3-E fail-closed stat arms are prose only | Stated bound B15 (no seam): `handleBoundToPath`'s two stat-failure arms and `verifyOwnership`'s `!ok` arm fail closed by code, unmeasured by test; reported as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors | — (bound, no code to kill) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B15 |\n31|| Obs-1 no-fallback proof covers `Dependencies.Spawn` only | Stated under B9: a fallback through direct `os/exec` is excluded today only by the import census (no `os/exec` import in the package) | — (bound) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B9 |\n32|| Obs-2 mode gate reads permission bits only | Stated bound B17: setgid/sticky on a 0700 leaf admitted, macOS ACLs uninspected — the landed `hosttrust` custody precedent (`platformModeOK`: `Perm() == mode`), same bound, not a fork | — (bound) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B17 |\n33|| Obs-3 derived socket unchecked against `sun_path` | Stated bound B18, owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz (lifecycle leaf adapter) | — (bound) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B18 |\n34|\n35|Kept untouched per the verdict: the dedicated-server rule per vector,\n36|the background broker-or-refuse wiring with the literal\n37|`capability_unavailable` and typed details, the no-fallback rule along\n38|the caller/credential/platform axes, the landed-admission attestation\n39|composition, the custody gates that held under attack, the\n40|FIFO/symlink/mode/UID/handle-mismatch refusals, the real-SIGKILL\n41|crash test, the determinism design (no real-tmux witness), and the\n42|`internal/traceability` boundary.\n43|\n44|## Deliverable (rev3 shape; production correct at every point, tests + one gate decision + prose)\n45|\n46|`internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked) —\n47|rev2 shape plus exactly one production-line change (P3-C):\n48|\n49|- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` with\n50|  three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership).\n51|  Foreground acquisition ensures idempotently; background acquisition\n52|  verifies the existing directory and never creates it. The verify\n53|  `Openat` carries `O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY` and no `O_NONBLOCK` by\n54|  decision (row 5).\n55|- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive the one\n56|  `-S` socket and refuse overrides and ambient collisions on all five\n57|  members (TMUX env, TMUX_TMPDIR, inherited socket, default path,\n58|  conventional name); collisions compare cleaned spellings, symlink\n59|  aliases bound.\n60|- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` refuses malformed input, ambient reuse,\n61|  and missing dependencies before any side effect. Foreground attaches\n62|  or spawns; background brokers-or-refuses with the typed\n63|  `capability_unavailable` and no fallback (the miss path consults the\n64|  creation gate by call; every background test arms a zero-call spy).\n65|- (4) Readiness: `CheckServerAttested` / `CheckBrokerContact` decide\n66|  the landed admission (`Admitted.Has(realm)` + generation equality)\n67|  over a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal, including\n68|  the both-empty pair on the exported helpers (entry-unreachable\n69|  through `Acquire`, where typed-details refuses an empty Generation\n70|  first). A stale admission — the replayed-cached shape — refuses on\n71|  both paths.\n72|- (5) Spawn argv: `BuildArgv` emits exactly\n73|  `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session`\n74|  through the landed argv gate. Native Windows refuses every request.\n75|\n76|Extended vs deliberately not extended (unchanged from rev2; the\n77|reviewer verified each claim rather than accepting it):\n78|\n79|- Extended (composed): `terminalbackend.Admitted` (attestation\n80|  verdict), `axpane` caller vocabulary, `axerror` typed refusal,\n81|  `scalar` platform/path/UUIDv7 grammars, `secprim` Guard /\n82|  `OpenNoFollowDir` / `CheckArgv`, the `hosttrust` verify-never-repair\n83|  precedent, the `termbind` crash-hook pattern.\n84|- Deliberately not extended: `hosttrust` custody itself (Host Channel\n85|  authority — a tmux runtime dir is not a trust store);\n86|  `terminalbackend` Reconcile evidence admission (consumed, not\n87|  re-owned); `axpane` checkRealm (unexported; this leaf composes the\n88|  same Has-plus-generation-equality over the probe-reported verdict);\n89|  the host-binding/provider-build cross-bind (stays with the lifecycle\n90|  owner, bound B13); `terminstance` lifecycle execution (sibling leaf);\n91|  `secprim`'s private `guardRootMatches` (mirrored as\n92|  `handleBoundToPath` with a seam because the original is unexported);\n93|  `internal/traceability` (untouched — bindings and the re-pin belong\n94|  to the final leaf).\n95|\n96|Determinism: every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs\n97|through injected dependencies. No test starts a tmux process; the\n98|suite passes with the tmux binary unresolvable and no tmux process on\n99|the host (64 top-level PASS, 0 SKIP in the tmux-hidden run). No AC row\n100|has a real-tmux witness — that is the design, not a gap (bound B1).\n101|\n102|## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\n103|\n104|**55 of 55 AC rows driven** through production entries by named\n105|committed tests — matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`,\n106|reproduced with spec-clause mapping in\n107|`TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md` (rev3). Row 5 now names\n108|both custody entries plus the background `Acquire`; rows 4, 23, 36,\n109|38 name the new pinning tests; the mutant-to-gate map names all 46\n110|narrowing rows.\n111|\n112|## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\n113|\n114|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py` —\n115|46 narrowing + 1 supplementary additive (D-background-fallback,\n116|labeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **48/48\n117|each, verdict lists identical**, exit 0. Per-row raw logs (go output +\n118|subprocess exit) for both passes are in the evidence tarball;\n119|production blobs byte-identical before/after every run\n120|(`git status` shows only candidate paths). No token-preserving\n121|source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text (stated\n122|bound B4, harness executes the behavioral suite). The one\n123|nil-dependency narrowing that kills by panic (N-deps-foreground) is\n124|disclosed in the harness and the matrix; N-deps-background kills by a\n125|custody-code mismatch since the admitted request reaches Verify.\n126|N-fchmod-umask assumes a non-root test user (bound B14), the same\n127|shape as the reviewer's plant. N-broker-empty-generation kills by\n128|reroute (server-generation detail mismatch), disclosed in its row\n129|note. The rev2 error-arm plant class (stat-failure arms flipped to\n130|fail-open) is reported as error-arm rows under bound B15 and is never\n131|counted among the narrowing survivors.\n132|\n133|## Crash / idempotency (unchanged from rev2)\n134|\n135|Real SIGKILL seam (unix): `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates`\n136|(child runs the genuine `EnsureRuntimeDir` entry and kills itself in\n137|`AfterMkdir`, after mkdirat and before verification plus parent\n138|fsync; parent proves the retry converges to the one verified\n139|directory). Idempotent replay: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`,\n140|`TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`,\n141|`TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry` (spawn-then-retry\n142|attaches with exactly one spawn). Crash convergence states the umask\n143|bound B10; the server socket's crash evidence is owned by the\n144|lifecycle leaf (bound B9).\n145|\n146|## Validation (all run firsthand in this session)\n147|\n148|Configured suite read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`\n149|(count 30, verified by read). All 30 green, run by this run (nothing\n150|accepted from rev2 or from construction):\n151|\n152|- 1 gofmt clean; 2 `go build ./...` exit 0; 3 `go vet ./...` exit 0.\n153|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v` exit 0: 45/45 packages ok, 0 package\n154|  FAIL, 0 unindented test FAIL (the 21 indented `--- FAIL` lines are\n155|  mutant-kill excerpts logged by the passing resumesmoke suite), 14\n156|  pre-existing SKIP outside this package, 0 SKIP in\n157|  `internal/tmuxserver`.\n158|- 5 race gate exit 0 with no DATA RACE: run in 6 bounded groups\n159|  (8/8/8/8/8/5 packages = all 45 from `go list ./...`) because one\n160|  shell call is time-bounded; same flags otherwise (`-race -count=1`).\n161|- 6 `go test ./... -cover -count=1` exit 0: 45/45 ok.\n162|  `go test ./internal/tmuxserver/ -cover` 91.6% statements.\n163|- 7-23 all 17 fuzz seeds exit 0. 24 tracecheck exit 0 (70/574).\n164|  25 cataloggen -check exit 0. 26 linux build exit 0. 27 windows build\n165|  exit 0. 28 JSON parse exit 0. 29 `task-board validate` exit 0 (with\n166|  the board's pre-existing 180 issues). 30 `git diff --check` exit 0.\n167|- Repository gates beyond the 30: `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet\n168|  ./...` exit 0 (P1-A proof, kept green); tmux-hidden suite\n169|  (`PATH` without tmux, `TMUX`/`TMUX_TMPDIR` unset, no tmux process)\n170|  exit 0 with 0 SKIP.\n171|\n172|Reran myself: everything above, plus the mutant battery (targeted\n173|subsets during development + two full logged passes). Accepted from\n174|already-attached evidence: nothing — rev2 evidence is superseded by\n175|this revision.\n176|\n177|`internal/traceability` untouched; README battery count updated to 46\n178|narrowing rows with exact test commands and no CLI/capability claim;\n179|LOGBOOK rev1 block folded into rev2 (F1-F3 preserved, stale bullets\n180|replaced with a SUPERSEDED pointer) plus one newest-first rev3 entry.\n181|The candidate is UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n182|\n183|## Rejection-pattern self-check\n184|\n185|(a) Literals asserted from spec text at entries (`capability_unavailable`\n186|plus all five typed details, exit 6; `ax`/`pane`/UUID session tail;\n187|`0700` on both the widened and narrower sides; caller vocabulary;\n188|`credential_capable_execution_realm` as the admitted member, including\n189|the both-empty pair), never production constants. (b) Every rule driven\n190|through the entry the matrix names; the creation gate is enforced by a\n191|call on the background miss path, custody refusals are staged through\n192|`Acquire` on both paths (including the verify-side non-directory leaf\n193|on the background entry), and the collision normalization is driven at\n194|both `ResolveSocket` and `Acquire`. (c) Landed owners composed (listed\n195|above) — only package-specific rules are new; the rev1 fork stays\n196|deleted. (d) Inputs driven, effects asserted (spy call counts, argv\n197|bytes, socket equality, typed details, attach vs refuse on stale vs\n198|bound admissions, deadline-bounded FIFO refusal); no census stands in\n199|for behavior. (e) 46 narrowing rows + labeled additive + applied\n200|SURVIVED control, one raw log per plant per run,\n201|narrowing-vs-additive stated per row; error-arm rows reported\n202|separately, never counted as narrowings. (f) Every \"never/composes\"\n203|sentence is backed by a failing-without test or stated as an explicit\n204|bound (B1-B18).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
