{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c79b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":552,"recorded_at":1780531400001099,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c45c-3a3b-7131-8103-0472dc0ac51e"},"task_id":"01a0c45c-3a3b-7131-8103-0472dc0ac51e","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"01a0c45c-3a3b-7131-8103-0472dc0ac51e","span_id":"931fd8be239dd335"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c79d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":553,"recorded_at":1780531400001101,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c45c-3a1f-7160-b02b-c51183a0471f"},"task_id":"01a0c45c-3a1f-7160-b02b-c51183a0471f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c45c-3a1f-7160-b02b-c51183a0471f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(759 line(s) above)\n760|13.13 adds a conformance gate over those flows, not a new component or sequence\n761|topology. Those rendered artifacts MUST NOT add relationships absent from this\n762|document or depict the derived index, display text, Directory Node, or\n763|enrichment worker as session, workspace, native-store, or lease authority.\n764|\n765|### 3.2 Platform paths\n766|\n767|Every path class has one exact command flag and environment override. Path\n768|resolution MUST use this precedence: the corresponding command flag, the\n769|corresponding non-empty environment override, then the platform default. A\n770|resolved file or directory MUST be absolute before use.\n771|\n772|| Path class | Command flag | Environment override | Value kind |\n773|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n774|| Configuration file | <code>--config PATH</code> | <code>AX_CONFIG</code> | Existing regular file, or a not-yet-created regular-file path whose parent exists |\n775|| Durable data root | <code>--data-dir PATH</code> | <code>AX_DATA_DIR</code> | Directory |\n776|| Mutable state root | <code>--state-dir PATH</code> | <code>AX_STATE_DIR</code> | Directory |\n777|| Cache root | <code>--cache-dir PATH</code> | <code>AX_CACHE_DIR</code> | Directory |\n778|| Runtime root | <code>--runtime-dir PATH</code> | <code>AX_RUNTIME_DIR</code> | Directory |\n779|\n780|This five-row table is the complete environment-override registry for version\n781|1.0.0. Empty values are treated as unset. An unknown variable beginning\n782|<code>AX_</code> is ordinary process environment and MUST NOT be interpreted by\n783|the configuration or path resolver. On native Windows, the runtime root stores\n784|owner-only transient metadata used to derive per-user named-pipe and process-\n785|handle names; the override never names a pipe directly.\n786|\n787|| Purpose | macOS | Linux and WSL2 | Native Windows |\n788|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n789|| Config | <code>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ax</code>, default <code>~/.config/ax</code> | Same | <code>%APPDATA%\\ax</code> |\n790|| Durable data | <code>~/Library/Application Support/ax</code> | <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/ax</code>, default <code>~/.local/share/ax</code> | <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\ax\\data</code> |\n791|| Mutable state/index | <code>~/Library/Application Support/ax/state</code> | <code>$XDG_STATE_HOME/ax</code>, default <code>~/.local/state/ax</code> | <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\ax\\state</code> |\n792|| Cache | <code>~/Library/Caches/ax</code> | <code>$XDG_CACHE_HOME/ax</code>, default <code>~/.cache/ax</code> | <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\ax\\cache</code> |\n793|| Runtime IPC | per-user temporary directory with mode 0700 | <code>$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax</code> | per-user named pipe and process handles |\n794|\n795|The XDG variables displayed in the defaults table are inputs to platform\n796|defaults, not additional <code>AX_*</code> overrides. On Windows, path\n797|comparison MUST use a\n798|volume-aware, case-insensitive comparison unless the volume is proven\n799|case-sensitive. On Unix, paths are byte-case-sensitive after UTF-8 validation.\n800|\n801|Ax-owned config, durable-data, state, cache, staging, and runtime directories\n802|MUST be accessible only to the current user: mode 0700 directories and 0600\n803|files on Unix, or a user-only DACL on Windows. Materialized workspace entries\n804|use their manifest modes, but their staging root remains user-only until commit.\n805|\n806|On macOS the tmux backend MUST use a dedicated AX server selected by\n807|<code>tmux -S &lt;runtime&gt;/tmux/ax.sock</code>. The\n808|<code>&lt;runtime&gt;/tmux</code> parent MUST be AX-created, owned by the current\n809|user, mode 0700, and verified component-by-component without following a\n810|symlink. Before bind, connect, rename, or unlink, AX MUST reject a socket path,\n811|parent, or ancestor whose resolved identity changed or whose file kind,\n812|ownership, or permissions are unsafe. The socket is runtime IPC, never durable\n813|identity.\n814|\n815|The durable data layout is:\n816|\n817|~~~text\n818|<data>/\n819|  objects/sha256/HH/REST\n820|  records/json/sha256/HH/REST\n821|  records/cbor/sha256/HH/REST\n822|  directory-records/json/sha256/HH/REST\n823|  directory-records/cbor/sha256/HH/REST\n824|  manifests/json/sha256/HH/REST\n825|  manifests/cbor/sha256/HH/REST\n826|  sessions/<session-id>/refs/\n827|  workspaces/<workspace-group-id>/refs/\n828|  staging/<transfer-id>/\n829|  quarantine/sha256/HH/REST/<quarantine-id>\n830|<state>/\n831|  index.sqlite\n832|  directory-jobs/<job-id>/refs/\n833|  directory-operations/<operation-id>/refs/\n834|  materializations/<materialization-id>.json\n835|  provider-object-sources/<materialization-id>/<provider-id>/\n836|  provider-transactions/<provider-id>/<transaction-id>/\n837|  managed-replicas/<managed-replica-id>/current.json\n838|  managed-replicas/<managed-replica-id>/markers/sha256/HH/REST.json\n839|  task-board-staging/<operation-id>/\n840|  service/\n841|~~~\n842|\n843|Every digest-derived durable path uses one function,\n844|<code>digest_path_v1(sha256:H) = sha256/H[0:2]/H[2:64]</code>, where H is the\n845|digest's exact 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. <code>HH</code> is therefore\n846|two characters and <code>REST</code> is the remaining 62; neither contains the\n847|<code>sha256:</code> prefix, and a full 64-character digest is never repeated as\n848|the leaf. Native Windows joins the same three components with backslashes, so\n849|no colon is placed in a filename. The rule is identical to the Object Sink and\n850|Task-board Bundle member rule; no storage class may choose a different split.\n851|\n852|Files under\n853|<code>objects</code>, <code>records</code>, and <code>manifests</code> MUST be\n854|immutable after successful creation. JSON and CBOR paths MAY coexist for one\n855|logical digest; both MUST decode to the same canonical JSON identity. A hash\n856|mismatch or representation disagreement MUST quarantine the file.\n857|\n858|A quarantined input is stored create-new beneath the digest path using a\n859|UUIDv7 <code>quarantine-id</code>; its digest directory may therefore retain\n860|multiple conflicting byte sequences without overwrite. The marker history\n861|path applies <code>digest_path_v1</code> to <code>marker_id</code> and appends\n862|<code>.json</code> only to REST. These golden paths are normative:\n863|\n864|| Digest/use | POSIX path suffix | Native Windows path suffix |\n865|| --- | --- | --- |\n866|| Empty-byte blob <code>sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855</code> | <code>objects/sha256/e3/b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855</code> | <code>objects\\sha256\\e3\\b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855</code> |\n867|| Example blob <code>sha256:9c21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50</code> | <code>objects/sha256/9c/21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50</code> | <code>objects\\sha256\\9c\\21bad65c1b3d0403ac85d7d5bd134bb8d894432702a396a77b0477b8eb3b50</code> |\n868|| Marker <code>sha256:385c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c</code> | <code>markers/sha256/38/5c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c.json</code> | <code>markers\\sha256\\38\\5c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c.json</code> |\n869|\n870|<code>PATH-DIGEST-N1</code> uses the full digest as REST,\n871|<code>PATH-DIGEST-N2</code> includes <code>sha256:</code> in a filename,\n872|<code>PATH-DIGEST-N3</code> uses the wrong shard, and\n873|<code>PATH-DIGEST-N4</code> gives JSON and CBOR representations different\n874|logical digests. Each MUST fail before durable installation.\n875|\n876|The two provider directories under <code>&lt;state&gt;</code> are created only by\n877|the destination <code>ax</code> host. They are never accepted as paths supplied\n878|by a peer or plugin. Section 7.5 defines their closed authorities, layouts,\n879|same-filesystem checks, retention, and cleanup. They MUST be path-disjoint from\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
