er or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\\n2345-stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\\n2346-verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\\n2347-already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\\n2348-and otherwise returns the typed `capability_unavailable` refusal with\\n2349-realm/readiness details — there is no fallback to direct creation, and\\n2350-every background test arms a spy spawner that fails the run if it is\\n2351-ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\\n2352-Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\\n2353-composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\\n2354-stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\\n2355-live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\\n2356-runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\\n2357-process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request.\\n2358-\\n2359-Run the focused tests and coverage with:\\n2360-\\n2361-```bash\\n2362-go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n2363-go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n2364-```\\n2365-\\n2366-Run the narrowing battery (46 narrowing mutants, one supplementary\\n2367-additive row, plus one harmless control) with:\\n2368-\\n2369-```bash\\n2370-PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n2371-```\\n2372-\\n2373-The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\\n2374-through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\\n2375-reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\\n2376-additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\\n2377-raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\\n2378-attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\\n2379-`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\\n2380-matrix with its stated bounds lives in\\n2381-[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n2382-\\n2383-## Ownership reducer properties\\n2384-\\n2385-The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\\n2386-and 13.6-13.10) hold as executable property tests over the landed production\\n2387-reducers — `sessstate.Reduce` with `Compare` and the union projection,\\n2388-`sessrepo.WinningLease` with `ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`:\\n2389-\\n===LOCALSTORE===\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tErr:    fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: %s: %v\\\", ErrInvalidPath, definition.Class, parseErr),\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tresolved.paths[definition.Class] = ResolvedPath{Class: definition.Class, Value: absolute, Source: source}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn resolved, nil\\n}\\n\\nfunc platformDefault(request ResolveRequest, class PathClass) (string, error) {\\n\\tjoin := func(elements ...string) string { return joinPlatform(request.Platform, elements...) }\\n\\tswitch request.Platform {\\n\\tcase scalar.PlatformMacOS:\\n\\t\\tif class == PathRuntime {\\n\\t\\t\\ttemporary, err := requireAbsoluteInput(request.Platform, \\\"temporary directory\\\", request.TemporaryDir)\\n\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(temporary, \\\"ax\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\thome, err := requireAbsoluteInput(request.Platform, \\\"home directory\\\", request.HomeDir)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tswitch class {\\n\\t\\tcase PathConfig:\\n\\t\\t\\tconfigBase, err := optionalAbsoluteEnvironment(request, \\\"XDG_CONFIG_HOME\\\", join(home, \\\".config\\\"))\\n\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(configBase, \\\"ax\\\", \\\"config.toml\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\tcase PathData:\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(home, \\\"Library\\\", \\\"Application Support\\\", \\\"ax\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\tcase PathState:\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(home, \\\"Library\\\", \\\"Application Support\\\", \\\"ax\\\", \\\"state\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\tcase PathCache:\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(home, \\\"Library\\\", \\\"Caches\\\", \\\"ax\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\tcase scalar.PlatformLinux, scalar.PlatformWSL2:\\n\\t\\tif class == PathRuntime {\\n\\t\\t\\truntimeBase, present := environmentValue(request, \\\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\\\")\\n\\t\\t\\tif !present || runtimeBase == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\\\", ErrPathDefaultUnavailable)\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tif _, err := requireAbsoluteInput(request.Platform, \\\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\\\", runtimeBase); err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(runtimeBase, \\\"ax\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\thome, err := requireAbsoluteInput(request.Platform, \\\"home directory\\\", request.HomeDir)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tswitch class {\\n\\t\\tcase PathConfig:\\n\\t\\t\\tbase, err := optionalAbsoluteEnvironment(request, \\\"XDG_CONFIG_HOME\\\", join(home, \\\".config\\\"))\\n\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn join(base, \\\"ax\\\", \\\"config.toml\\\"), nil\\n\\t\\tcase PathData:\\n\\t\\t\\tbase, err := optionalAbsoluteEnvironment(request, \\\"XDG_DATA_HOME\\\", join(home, \\\".local\\\", \\\"share\\\"))\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5670,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1418,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
