{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caa5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c45a-c3aa-73a1-9c84-6d5fc23e6787"},"sequence":941,"recorded_at":1780531400001877,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"892d0e23-8edf-4e7b-8430-1bc89cf9b07d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c45d-3daa-7df1-a90d-1f54d729448f"},"task_id":"01a0c45d-3daa-7df1-a90d-1f54d729448f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c45d-3daa-7df1-a90d-1f54d729448f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-15-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 60 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"===\\\"; grep -n \\\"ax-tmux\\\\|Runtime IPC\\\\|state root\\\\|State root\\\" internal/tmuxserver/*.go internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md README.md | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK head and path references\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev3 — Private tmux server management rework (verify-side non-directory pin, both-empty arms, narrower-mode pin, cleaned collision)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2, five P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev1 finding stays closed). P2-A: the verify-side non-directory refusal is now pinned on the entry the background path uses — `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` (0700 regular file admitted outright under the mutant; FIFO under a 5s deadline so the no-hang property pins too) plus `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` through the background entry, with harness row `N-containment-odirectory-verify` (kill signature: err-nil on both entries, 5s FIFO stall). Deliberate gate decision: the verify `Openat` carries no `O_NONBLOCK` — FIFO refusal relies on `O_DIRECTORY` failing fast, symmetric with the commit side, stated in TRACEABILITY row 5.\\n- P3-A: both-empty generation rows in both readiness tables plus `N-realm-empty-want` / `N-broker-empty-generation` (the broker row kills by reroute to the server-generation detail, disclosed in its note). P3-B: the narrower side of \\\"exactly 0700\\\" pinned — a pre-existing 0600/0500 leaf refuses `runtime mode` on both entries (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode`, `N-mode-narrower-create/verify`), so the exact-0700 prose stands as written. P3-C: the collision gate compares `filepath.Clean` spellings (one production-line change; `/./` and `//` aliases refused at `ResolveSocket` and through `Acquire`, `N-collision-unclean` drops `Clean`; symlink aliases bound B16). P3-D: the rev1 LOGBOOK block folded into rev2 (F1-F3 preserved, stale bullets replaced with a SUPERSEDED pointer). P3-E: stat-failure arms stated as bound B15 (error-arm rows, never counted as narrowings). Observations: import-census no-fallback bound under B9, Perm-only mode bound B17 (hosttrust precedent), `sun_path` bound B18 owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz.\\n- Battery: 46 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 48/48 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev3; row 5 names both entries, rows 4/23/36/38 name the new pins). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in 6 bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 64 pass / 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev2 — Private tmux server management rework (P1 attestation fork + Windows vet, 9 surviving narrowings)\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev1 (CHANGES REQUESTED: 2 P1, 4 P2, 4 P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh). P1-A: `runtime_test.go` now carries `//go:build !windows` (it reassigns the unix-only `effectiveUID` seam and uses `syscall.Umask`); `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` is green (exit 0, run firsthand). P1-B: the forked `LiveAttestation`/`CachedObservation`/`ManagerNameHint`/`BrokerStatus` model is DELETED — `RealmAdmission` consumes the landed `terminalbackend.Admitted` verdict composed only with the `RawGeneration == Generation` equality `axpane.checkRealm` enforces, and the broker principal is a typed same-user UID plus generation-bound generation (no bare boolean); `Request.Hint`/`Cached`/`NeedsCredentials` are deleted with no replacement fields. The three reviewer holes now refuse through `Acquire`: wrong-generation foreground attach, wrong-generation broker contact, and a stale admission (the replayed-cached shape) on both paths.\\n- P2-A: nine surviving narrowings closed with committed killers + shipped rows — `Acquire` commit-phase refusal (`TestAcquireForegroundStagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-commit-refusal), background verify wiring (`TestAcquireBackgroundStagesVerifyCustodyRefusal`, N-acquire-verify-refusal), verify-side symlink leaf (N-containment-symlink-verify), `TMUX_TMPDIR` override as the fifth vector (row 55, N-override-tmpdir), per-member collisions through `Acquire` (N-collision ×4), TMUX-env argv member (N-argv-tmuxenv), umask-0177 create proving the explicit `Fchmod` (N-fchmod-umask); the unreachable `ObserveAmbient` vocabulary arm is deleted. P2-B: `PlatformWindows` refuses at the lexical gate on every host (`tmux_invalid_arguments`); the Windows commit/verify arms are refusal stubs and the tripwire is deleted. P2-C: the decision-core-only split is a stated bound (B9, exec/probe adapters + socket crash evidence owned by TASK-260830-1c28dz) and the \\\"production wires\\\" sentence is deleted. P2-D: background acquisition verifies instead of ensuring (no durable write on the authorizing path); the dead foreground `checkCreationAllowed` call is deleted.\\n- P3: results now read the 30 commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` and report firsthand runs; crash convergence states the umask bound (B10); symlinked root intermediates state the secprim-matching bound (B11); the `CheckArgv` arm is covered by direct call with its Acquire-unreachability bound (B12). Battery: 40 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, twice with per-plant raw logs. AC: 55 of 55 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev2). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- FINDINGS carried forward from the rejected rev1 tree (the rev1 LOGBOOK block below is superseded and folded here; its DELIVERED/mutation/AC/bounds bullets described code deleted before trunk): F1 — a structural absence (\\\"this path has no spawn call\\\") is not an enforceable gate until a call exists to weaken, so the background miss path consults `checkCreationAllowed` by call (N-creation-literal reddens with the creation code, D-background-fallback reddens on the spy assertions). F2 — `Fchmod` before verification silently repairs, so the create path chmods only leaves it created while pre-existing leaves verify as-is (a widened `0755` refuses on both ensure and verify). F3 — single-member refusal classes narrow honestly (`caller == \\\"background\\\"` weakens to the capitalized twin; delegated scalar/secprim wirings narrow at our call site with reroute kills, never by re-testing the owner).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev1 (SUPERSEDED by the rev2 entry above — describes the rejected rev1 tree, never landed)\\n\\n- The rev1 block's DELIVERED/mutation/AC/bounds bullets are deleted: `CheckLiveAttestation`, four ambient vectors, the Windows creating-user ACL tripwire, 29 mutants, 54/54 rows, and 87.5% coverage describe the rejected rev1 design. Its findings F1-F3 are preserved in the rev2 entry above.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): P1-a CLOSED — envelope+body frame decodes delegate to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (lone-surrogate/duplicate/trailing faults refuse with the fault named; the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate); 4 new refusal rows + 4 narrowings. P2-c CLOSED — `bodyUint53` and the envelope version delegate to `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` (string-typed numbers refuse; per-member failures merge into one \\\"is not a uint53\\\" refusal while the ledger sum keeps \\\"exceeds uint53\\\"); string rows + 5 narrowings. New P3 rows: actor-order determinism (3 actors x12, `N-actors-sort`), both type/protection agreement arms, trailing bytes, protected-tool fold-skip, result-status vocabulary, size arm with its own message + drift row, unknown+protected body refusal; P3-i non-JSONL bound stated + pinned, P3-l null-directives pinned, P3-c per-edge rows stated as bounds (the \\\"representative\\\" claim removed); P3-j unions the 10.2 binding to 11 cases (10.2#2 gains `localstore-immutable-blob-install`); P3-k relabels (`N-empty-projection` single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap). P2-a: one decision line per inherited advisory group (1,2,3,5,6,7b deferred with owners; 4/P3-e closed as a stated bound; 7a/P3-ζ closed by P1-a; 7c/P3-ζ′ rewritten as a deferred-unification bound) and the two false-prose sites rewritten. P2-b: 7.8#1 rebound to the new `session-adapter-frame-bound` case (`DecodeRequestFrame` + the oversize/edge tests, sessadapter owner); cases 144→145; digest re-derived `4bd01143…` gate-computed;