+ fold-first narrowing); P3-o external kind pinned (`TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` + kind narrowing, and the reviewer-exact R7 swap KILLED firsthand); P3-p unknown-type-without-body refusal row + required-member narrowing (reviewer R1 shape); P3-q `text:null` stated as a bound (seals empty inline content, pinned) with `ciphertext:null` noted harmless; P3-r `N-pending-aborted` relabelled add-arm and the shared-site `N-strict-*` rows disclosed as one gate/two call sites (harness + TRACEABILITY + matrix + results); P3-s per-edge bound text now names `native_type` (reviewer R2 re-run firsthand: SURVIVED, inside the bound). Five prose sites corrected (`native.go` comments, TRACEABILITY rows, README exact-name sentence, this entry, results).\\n- REV3 EVIDENCE: 72 narrowing + 3 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; reviewer R1/R4/R5/R6 shapes adopted as shipped narrowings, R7 adopted as a condition narrowing with the exact swap also KILLED firsthand, R3 still KILLED (untouched line). AC: 45 of 45 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev3).\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260918-d009f2, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the rev2 rework is CLOSED AT THE CLASS per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched): P2-e CLOSED — `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets` resolves EVERY event's `RawRefs[0]` against its own line with offsets asserted (`0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2`, multibyte first line), plus labelled behaviour-swap `N-offset-newline`; the reviewer's `RV-offset-line-number` and `RV-evidence-offset-second-line` shapes KILLED firsthand by the new row. P3-u/z pinned as bounds (`TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse`, `TestNormalizeUnknownTypeNullBodyProjectsOpaque`); P3-v rows shipped (`body_text_number`, `body_live_attestation_string`, `body_missing_text` + 3 narrowings, the required gate pinned by its message); P3-w low edge pinned (`empty_directive` + `N-directive-empty`); P3-x `doc.go` nine→ten; P3-y declined-cosmetic with rationale (uniform member+line error shape is AC-pinned; the clonebundle helper wording at `session.go:527` is accepted sibling production, behavior verified correct); P3-aa MANIFEST self-entry dropped. No production change: test-plus-matrix only.\\n- REV4 REFRESH: trunk moved `c3aae73`→`42d5a95` (sibling STORY-260830-ptxkqe landed) before this run, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `42d5a95`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay for both checkpoints); the audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/fencing`, `internal/terminalbackend`) and MERGED the five co-owned files (LOGBOOK newest-first, README figures+prose, ownership registry 152 cases/74 rows with every trunk row intact, the four pin tests); `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-derived via the gate as `614eb55d…` (command+output in results); `tracecheck` green `70/574` with `--section 7.8`/`10.2` admitted. AC: 47 of 47 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev4).\\n- REV5 (rework of review RUN-260918-492d65, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the ENTIRE rev3 rework is CLOSED and the refresh was a verified MERGE per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched; trunk unmoved at `42d5a95`, no refresh): P2-f CLOSED — the AC-named scale far edges are driven, not delegated: 65-parent / 1025-head / 1025-actor / 1000001-event-ID refusal rows at build AND decode in `internal/clonebundle` (each asserting code + message; otherwise-valid inputs so every build-side widening kills by admission), 8 widening narrowings (one per build/decode site, incl. the decode-actors row's missing narrowing), matrix section D and `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md` citing rows by name. P3-bb unterminated multi-line tail row (last event + offset asserted) + labelled drop row; P3-cc two per-type registry rows (`live_followup` on a call, `live_attestation` on a result) + narrowings with a seven-site census in results (the verdict says six; the tree carries seven maps); P3-dd output-axis usage overflow row + narrowing; P3-ee decode-side distinct-unsorted `raw_refs` row + narrowing; P3-ff CRLF stated beside the terminator sentence and pinned by a test; P3-gg matrix test-name fix + `forty-seven` dropped from the pin-test number map; P3-hh empty `subagent:` row + narrowing (honest message pin: the plant still refuses at the actor mapping). No production change: test-plus-matrix only.\\n- REV5 EVIDENCE: cloneproject battery 86/86 `ok:` twice (80 narrowings + 5 labelled KILLED + control SURVIVED), clonebundle battery 76/76 twice (75 + control), clonesnap 44/44 once (unchanged package), one raw log per plant per run with subprocess exits; `tracecheck` green `70/574` with `--section 7.8`/`10.2` admitted and the `614eb55d…` pin re-proven by the zeroed-pin gate print; full 30-command suite green (race gate in 7 bounded groups, 44/44 packages, no DATA RACE; full suite 2796 top-level PASS, +2 new tests). AC: 47 of 47 rows driven (matrix rev5; rows 4/10/23 extended, section D rewritten to cite rows).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm rev3 — Binding-parser rework: closed-shape arms, identity pre-transform walk, stated bounds\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2-1 production at the Binding parser, five P3; the reviewer reproduced the v4 payloads, evidence/identity/recovery/authority behavior, the registry re-pin, and the harness 30/30 twice — all kept). P2-1: `ParseTerminalBinding` now enforces `protocol_version` major 1 (`isProtocolMajorOne` over the landed semver grammar, verdict-agreed with `CheckVersionTuple` on a 14-version corpus) and `extensions == {}` (landed strict frame, zero members) per the §4.B table, and `bindingIdentity` refuses JSON numbers at any depth plus nested duplicate members before the JCS transform (strict UseNumber decode with per-depth dup refusal, mirroring the landed terminalbackend decode+walk — digest-equality and verdict agreement pinned, including a numeric extension value). Every member arm of the table is now driven negatively through the entry (37-subtest battery with code+detail pins) with six new narrowing rows (major, extensions, number, nested-dup, supersedes, pre-read generation bound). P3-2: `EmitResumed` checkpoint/pair binding stated explicitly as a caller bound with a boundary-pinning test (fabricated checkpoint appends; fold reports it newest). P3-3: generation-bound-before-read witness committed with its row. P3-4: pre-scan harness notes corrected to the documented redundancy, README bootstrap sentence corrected to the plain refusal, `resolve.go` \\\"every failure\\\" scoped to resolution failures, row 57 / 5.2#18 restated as a bound, descriptor test added to the identity-exact case. P3-5: restore/terminate-stale execution deferred to a Story follow-up task (no board task exists yet — no brief assigned it); the kkh1an `HandoffFailed` note is NOT APPLICABLE (this leaf wires no reporter).\\n- CORRECTION to the rev1 entry's F2 (appended, history preserved): \\\"the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals)\\\" is wrong for the two body surfaces — the landed `ParseMutationContext`/`ParseStatusBody` refuse a forbidden identity with the SAME pinned `terminal_backend_protocol_error`; the pre-scans add only the Go error type (`*terminalbackend.Error`), and no wrapper exists for the bootstrap surface at all (landed `Store.Bind` refuses plain and uncoded). The wrappers stay as a documented redundancy with corrected notes.\\n- F1: a major-1 selection over an already-validated semver needs no integer parse — the major is the digit run before the first dot, so prefix `1.` is exact with no saturation class for huge foreign majors; the 14-version agreement battery against `CheckVersionTuple` (grammar faults, majors 0/2/3/10, a 2^64-scale major, prerelease/build spellings) proves no second model.\\n- F2: `bindingIdentity`'s old \\\"no number can reach the digest by check ordering\\\" comment was false exactly where extension values are untyped — the pre-transform walk must be structural (decode + walk), not an ordering claim; the direct-identity hostile battery (numbers, nested dups, trailing data, depth/size caps) pins the walk independently of the member arms that now fire first.\\n- AC: 65 of 66 rows driven through production entries by named tests (row 57 restated as a bound — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk; rows 61–66 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`). MUTATION EVIDENCE: 34 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary arm-delete row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. Registry: 5.2 gap reworded to the row-57 bound, eight test citations added across four cases with mirror updates, digest re-derived `b09b5b9f…` (canonical bytes 167094), tracecheck green `63/574` with identical section ratios. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm rev2 — Race-gate rework: per-subtest evidence universes\\n- REWORKED after the rev1 CR validation stopped at command 5/30 (`go test ./... -race`): one DATA RACE in `TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` — four parallel subtests shared a single `mapUniverse` while the two \\\"second\\\" cases extended it, racing the sibling `Lookup` reads (`resolve_test.go:172/181` vs `fixtures_test.go:490`). The race detector then failed the whole `termbind` package; every other package was green. Fix is test-only: each subtest builds its own `universeMap(t, world)` copy (rev2 delta vs the rev1 candidate is exactly this hunk, proven by whole-tree diff of the reconstructed rev1 tree). No production byte changed; the `N-resolve-manifest-count` killer still kills its narrowing mutant.\\n- VERIFIED: `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` green (plus two more `-count=3` passes), siblings `axpane`/`terminstance` `-race` green, `mutant_harness.py` 30/30 on two identical passes, gofmt/vet/build clean, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical, trunk still `c3aae73` (no refresh). Full 30-command suite reruns automatically at handoff.\\n- F1: a shared mutable map across `t.Parallel()` subtests fails the entire package under `-race`, not just the racing test — every concurrently running test reports \\\"race detected during execution of test\\\", so one fixture race reads as fifteen failures. Fixture isolation per subtest is the fix; read-only sharing (as in `TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds`) stays safe.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/termbind` — the §4.1/4.B-4.D/5.2-Terminal-Events/7.A final leaf over the landed owners and the story's own `axpane`/`terminstance`: `ParseTerminalBinding` owns the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object no parser existed for (ID recomputed before use, construction byte-agreed with the landed manifest admission); `CheckInstanceIdentity` + the operation-body pre-scans refuse the eight forbidden identity forms with the pinned protocol class on the Binding, descriptor (adopted landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts, with the CLI Result 4 surface a tripwire-pinned bound; `ResolveEvidence` resolves each v4 event's evidence IDs to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through the landed `Registry.AdmitProbe` (eleven foreign resolution targets refuse, substitution fails closed); `EmitTerminalCreated`/`EmitResumed` author the v4 payloads under a locally held lease with the digest as the opaque reference; `RecoverCreate` is read-only (absence / ONE child / unavailable+status_first, window from the fold newest); the attach receipt store records one durable receipt per client pair and emits neither event. Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, never a fork; v1 readers stay inert.\\n- F1: the producer's \\\"§13.1\\\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the pinned v0.7.0 document (\\\"status plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one child\\\") — §13.1's eight measured clauses are launch-plan/boot-direct/argv rules owned by another story, so the registry binds `section:4.1` (new, sliver 1/5) and leaves `section:13.1` untouched, with the mapping stated in the results.\\n- F2: a pre-scan gate is masked wherever the landed parser refuses with the identical code — the descriptor surface needed no wrapper (landed `AdmitProviderDescriptor` already pins `terminal_backend_protocol_error`), while the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals), and same-code reroutes (transport enum, evidence protocol arm, foreign-kind classification) need detail assertions or the mutant survives behind the landed twin.\\n===\\ninternal/tmuxserver/acquire.go:83:\\t// state root, Name is the runtime leaf (usually\\ninternal/tmuxserver/runtime.go:12:// directory under the AX state root. It is AX-controlled vocabulary,\\ninternal/tmuxserver/runtime.go:14:const RuntimeDirName = \\\"ax-tmux\\\"\\ninternal/tmuxserver/socket.go:10:const SocketName = \\\"ax-tmux.sock\\\"\\ninternal/tmuxserver/tmuxserver_test.go:160:\\tif got := SocketPath(dir); got != filepath.Join(dir, \\\"ax-tmux.sock\\\") {\\ninternal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md:211:  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep state root surfaces as\\nREADME.md:1619:mode `0600` under the owner-only state root, and never appear beneath\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 28498,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 7125,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
